1
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,460
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,060
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:55,260
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:55,580 --> 00:00:57,340
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:01,820
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,100
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:06,340
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:08,380
(Wang Churan)

9
00:01:08,580 --> 00:01:10,420
(Song Yaxuan)

10
00:01:11,140 --> 00:01:15,860
=Natural High S4=

11
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,180
=EP6 (Part 2): Beneath the Great Wall=

12
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,280
Morning, Bing.

13
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:26,840
Hello.

14
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:29,080
Good morning.

15
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,360
That was a textbook "good morning".

16
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:33,440
Good morning.

17
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,360
What app did you open?

18
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:36,920
Good morning. I'm Churan.

19
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:38,520
I'd be happy

20
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:39,360
to guide you.

21
00:01:40,560 --> 00:01:41,640
I'm playing Bing's rap.

22
00:01:42,360 --> 00:01:42,880
Be good.

23
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:43,560
Okay?

24
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:44,200
Behave.

25
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:45,240
Love it.

26
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:46,880
Play.

27
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:51,800
♪Braved the north♪

28
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,000
♪Chasing my dreams♪

29
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:58,480
Churan, put your hands up.

30
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,200
Hard to get a good swing

31
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:02,160
at him in the car, huh?

32
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,560
♪Too flashy♪

33
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:07,960
♪Too wild♪

34
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,360
♪Every challenge♪

35
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,440
How'd I do, Teng?

36
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,200
I've listened to it a lot, right?

37
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,760
You memorized nine words.

38
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:19,880
And you're still fishing for praise.

39
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,200
Credit hog.

40
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,400
Can I ask you something,

41
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:25,880
Teng?

42
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:28,400
What's Bai's song called?

43
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,160
Just focus on driving.

44
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,320
Bai, happy birthday.

45
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:38,720
You know

46
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:39,640
the title of Bai's song?

47
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:40,840
It's right there.

48
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:41,520
Keep It Real.

49
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:43,800
How was I supposed to remember?

50
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:44,640
Bai, happy birthday.

51
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,560
They're treating me like
a parenthetical

52
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,500
(Something clicks)
aside.

53
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,200
They are treating you
like a parenthetical aside.

54
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:51,360
You know what?

55
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,680
I went to the Great Wall the other day.

56
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:53,520
Bai, happy birthday.

57
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,320
Then I opened...

58
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:56,300
(Another surprise birthday wish)

59
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,600
We took some pictures together.

60
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:00,360
Bai, happy birthday.

61
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,680
Looks like the river's dried up.

62
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,520
Bai, happy birthday.

63
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,000
(Too much birthday love)

64
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,000
That phrase

65
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:07,960
is so handy.

66
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,800
I'll be doing this all day, Bai.

67
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:10,840
(Another parenthetical-style line)

68
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:11,920
Keep it real.

69
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:13,080
(Now they're getting ideas)

70
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,000
Spring Festival couplets.

71
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:14,880
Keep it real.

72
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:16,600
Hang couplets, set off firecrackers.

73
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,320
Keep it real.

74
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,040
Bai, happy birthday.

75
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,260
(If you can't beat 'em, join 'em)
Keep it real.

76
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,640
Bai, you were up late last night, right?

77
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,400
Keep it real.

78
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:23,680
I was mad till 3AM.

79
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:25,380
(Still mad about last night)

80
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:27,360
Bai rolled his eyes all night.

81
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,480
(Eye exercises all night)

82
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,200
Even when he fell asleep,

83
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:30,600
his eyes stayed wide open.

84
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:33,360
(Snorting with laughter)

85
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,520
Couldn't rest in peace.

86
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:35,160
(Couldn't rest in peace?)

87
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:35,680
I was dying of anger.

88
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:36,820
(A tiny rage outburst)

89
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:38,560
Chengcheng, too.

90
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,200
He really acts

91
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:41,880
like he's so smart,

92
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,640
like the rest of us are stupid.

93
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:45,220
(Who's talking behind my back?)

94
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,800
Everyone else knew it was me.

95
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,800
Except him.

96
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:50,000
And he was losing his mind.

97
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,200
Then show it.

98
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:53,480
So annoying.

99
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,000
Bing, you should launch your own liquor.

100
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,760
(Showing off his smarts)
Your brand should be called

101
00:03:57,760 --> 00:03:58,400
Jia Booze.
[*Fake booze]

102
00:03:58,700 --> 00:03:59,740
(What a name)

103
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,920
We're filming in Beijing.

104
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:04,440
Don't wander off.

105
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,520
Once you leave Bai's turf,

106
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,080
it gets tricky for him.

107
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,320
Even dragons better coil up.

108
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,040
Even tigers better lie low.

109
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,880
You two sound so mushy.

110
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:18,660
(A mushy guy from Northeast China)

111
00:04:18,660 --> 00:04:19,420
(A mushy guy from Shandong)

112
00:04:19,420 --> 00:04:20,180
(A mushy guy from Tianjin)

113
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,830
Give it a few more days,

114
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,560
and the leaves

115
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,520
will all turn yellow.

116
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:27,720
Even prettier.

117
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:31,720
You can't take your eyes off it.

118
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,360
(Casually showing off)
Beijing's northernmost,

119
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,720
Huairou's the most beautiful.

120
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:37,880
You can say that again.

121
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,410
(Certified Beijing dialect expert)
Don't even get me started.

122
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,120
Don't even get me started, sir.

123
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:41,920
Just correcting you.

124
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:48,080
Don't look, Song.

125
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,240
Listen.

126
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:49,880
What vehicle is that?

127
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:51,600
A motorcycle.

128
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:52,760
Good.

129
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,760
Song actually knows

130
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:56,520
a thing or two about engines.

131
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:57,600
That last one

132
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:58,080
was a regular car.

133
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,120
A four-wheeler.

134
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:02,120
(When you're dying laughing
and your friend keeps it coming)

135
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,720
Sorry, sir. Couldn't tell.

136
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:08,880
Close your eyes and listen.

137
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:11,040
Hear that? What is it?

138
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,680
That was a motorcycle, really.

139
00:05:12,760 --> 00:05:13,760
That scared me.

140
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,120
That sound's terrifying.

141
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,040
Kids will be kids.

142
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:20,880
Back in our day...

143
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,040
(A Northeasterner who loves reminiscing)

144
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,400
We knew engines by sound.

145
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:25,240
There it goes.

146
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,840
What kind of car?

147
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:28,280
(The Beijing accent's out of control)
What engine size?

148
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:29,320
And the brand?

149
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,640
We Beijingers

150
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:33,920
don't actually talk like that.

151
00:05:33,920 --> 00:05:35,240
(Official disclaimer)
Don't listen to him.

152
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,760
Can you play some white noise?

153
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,560
Rain sounds?

154
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,520
You'll fall asleep.

155
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,640
I'll play something really soothing.

156
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,220
(Instant relaxation)

157
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:58,400
So beautiful.

158
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,320
Up ahead.

159
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,320
Really beautiful.

160
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:04,160
Are those terraced fields?

161
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:06,760
Terraced fields in Beijing?
Come on, Song.

162
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,560
They kinda look like it.

163
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,560
Stinky little bro.

164
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:11,200
Stinky?

165
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,040
Sweet big bro.

166
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,480
I'm your sweet big bro.

167
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:18,680
We're here.

168
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:20,320
Would you look at that.

169
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,200
Look.

170
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,920
The good times

171
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,280
always fly by.

172
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,040
Whoa.

173
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:30,440
This trunk holds a ton.

174
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,800
Bing, stop working so hard.

175
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,400
Come relax with me.

176
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,480
Teng, you're so laid-back.

177
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:36,800
Just like the Stelato V8's trunk.

178
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:37,400
Room for everything.

179
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,080
We're here to have fun.

180
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:38,880
Fun comes first.

181
00:06:38,880 --> 00:06:40,440
Come share my happiness.

182
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:42,000
These seats can slide together?

183
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:42,800
Of course.

184
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:43,640
Perfect.

185
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,040
Let's watch together.

186
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:54,920
Going all retro today?

187
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:56,400
(Today's retro outfit)
Yes.

188
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:58,400
Our car earlier

189
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,560
was so sappy I could barely
keep my eyes open.

190
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:05,240
Teng gave a 15-minute monologue.

191
00:07:05,260 --> 00:07:07,580
(A Northeasterner who loves monologues)

192
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:09,360
I'm getting old.

193
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,480
Can't stop rambling.

194
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:17,800
Yesterday, we climbed
the majestic Great Wall.

195
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:19,080
Today, we're

196
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:20,040
right at its foot.

197
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,400
And right now, Beijing,

198
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:22,520
just like Hu,

199
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,000
has finally reached

200
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,220
its prime.

201
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:27,480
Look at him

202
00:07:27,480 --> 00:07:29,000
showering Hu with compliments.

203
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:29,860
(He's gone full local, too)

204
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,520
Which bodybuilding champ is talking?

205
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:38,640
Today's game

206
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,350
is Undercover Werewolf.

207
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,600
(Undercover Werewolf)
There'll be seven Good Guys

208
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,560
and one Killer Zero.

209
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:45,480
Killer Zero

210
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,800
can't eliminate Good Guys directly,

211
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:48,600
but can infect any Good Guy

212
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:49,240
to become Killer One.

213
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:50,480
Killer One

214
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,520
can use a specific action

215
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:52,640
to eliminate Good Guys.

216
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:53,920
Good Guys can ring the gong anytime

217
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:55,920
(Fan Chengcheng)
to gather everyone for a discussion

218
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,200
and vote someone out.

219
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:58,640
The Good Guys win
by finishing their tasks

220
00:07:58,640 --> 00:07:59,960
or voting out Killer Zero.

221
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,920
Either way, they win.

222
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,250
(Jia Bing)
The rules are simple.

223
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,320
Everyone got it?

224
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,400
Got it.

225
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,960
If Killer Zero gets eliminated,

226
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:08,800
the game's over.

227
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:09,480
But if Killer One gets eliminated,

228
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,880
Zero can recruit another One.

229
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:11,360
Correct.

230
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:12,040
(Huang Jingyu)

231
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:12,800
So it's just Zero

232
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:13,240
and One.

233
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:13,800
No Two.

234
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,560
Only one Killer at a time?

235
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:17,080
Right.

236
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:17,640
Don't kill me.

237
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:20,720
(Bai Jingting)
How exactly does the Killer kill?

238
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,520
That's a secret.

239
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:22,600
You'll get it once we play.

240
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,800
Fair enough.

241
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,920
(Hu Xianxu)
Teng's completely lost it.

242
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,800
He's gone totally crazy.

243
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:29,120
Someone stop him.

244
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:32,640
Okay, let's draw our role cards.

245
00:08:32,940 --> 00:08:34,100
(Drawing roles)

246
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:37,860
(Good luck)

247
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:38,720
Give me Zero.

248
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:47,520
First thing in the morning...

249
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,360
Perfect.

250
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:50,920
Why'd I have to draw this?

251
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,720
Okay, everyone close your eyes.

252
00:08:57,680 --> 00:08:58,760
Now,

253
00:08:58,760 --> 00:09:00,920
Killer Zero, open your eyes.

254
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:03,100
(Killer Zero: Secret)

255
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,000
Who's Zero?

256
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,140
(Wang Churan)

257
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:09,200
Okay, everyone open your eyes.

258
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:11,960
(Killer Zero: Secret)
Your task this round is

259
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:12,520
to peel eggs.

260
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,560
In the game area,

261
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,880
there are ten task stations.

262
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,000
Once all seven plates

263
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,800
have peeled quail eggs on them,

264
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:22,000
the Good Guys complete their mission.

265
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,760
Now head to your starting points.

266
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,120
Can you add a teleport effect?

267
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,220
(Done. You're welcome)

268
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,880
Neighborhood security chief.

269
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,200
I think it's Teng.

270
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:46,440
(Song's got a theory)

271
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,000
Because earlier,

272
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,720
when they told Killer Zero
to open their eyes,

273
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:51,840
Teng suddenly started eating his dates

274
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:52,880
way more slowly.

275
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:54,920
Killer Zero, open your eyes.

276
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,140
(Clue spotted)

277
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,920
So I suspect Teng.

278
00:09:59,220 --> 00:10:01,200
(Teng's under suspicion)

279
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,440
What are you doing here?

280
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:04,060
(One suspiciously chatty Killer)

281
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:05,080
Just checking on you.

282
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,200
Seeing how you're doing.

283
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:09,080
You've got that much free time?

284
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:10,880
I think you and I

285
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:13,160
can safely say

286
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,040
we're both innocent.

287
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,080
I definitely am. You? Not so sure.

288
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:18,840
We're bored out of our minds.

289
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,600
What do you mean, not sure?

290
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,500
(Mission begins)

291
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,200
This is exciting.

292
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:25,440
Let's start.

293
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:26,440
Let's go.

294
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:28,280
The game's on.

295
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:31,440
Killer Zero, infect me.

296
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,340
(Job hunting at 33 be like)

297
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:36,560
♪I'd give up everything for you♪

298
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:37,560
Bai.

299
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,120
Bai,

300
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:40,680
happy birthday.

301
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,800
You're pushing 40, Bai.

302
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:44,560
(Thanks for the reminder)

303
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,560
There goes his good mood.

304
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:48,080
My mood's ruined.

305
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:50,520
Suddenly, today's not so sunny anymore.

306
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,120
Infect me.

307
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:58,560
Killer, infect me.

308
00:10:59,000 --> 00:10:59,720
Who's that?

309
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,080
Is it you? Infect me.

310
00:11:02,080 --> 00:11:02,920
Come on, infect me.

311
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,000
Nobody's watching.

312
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,300
(Please pick me, Mr. Killer)
Go ahead, infect me.

313
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:06,640
Okay.

314
00:11:06,920 --> 00:11:07,200
Okay.

315
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:08,700
(Is this my chance?)

316
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:16,760
Gotcha. I'm not the Killer.

317
00:11:16,760 --> 00:11:18,460
(Cheeky little rascal)

318
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:22,720
Don't kick me.

319
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:27,780
(Instantly joining the chaos)

320
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:30,620
(Witnessing a mysterious ritual)

321
00:11:30,860 --> 00:11:32,780
(Something's fishy about them)

322
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,680
Bai and Song

323
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,330
(A huge misunderstanding)
were exchanging secret signals.

324
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,520
I saw the whole thing.

325
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,680
(Off to investigate)

326
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:48,600
Hi.

327
00:11:49,440 --> 00:11:50,160
Infect me.

328
00:11:50,860 --> 00:11:52,100
(You're my prime suspect)

329
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,160
You're not the Killer either?

330
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:53,760
Nope.

331
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:56,720
Find a spot and pretend to swim.

332
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:57,680
Then you'll get your ammo.

333
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:01,680
Killer Zero, open your eyes.

334
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:03,540
(Killer Zero)

335
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,800
(Swim with Killer One for 15 seconds)
To get ammo, we both have

336
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,580
(Killer One then gains the power to attack)
to pretend to swim on the floor.

337
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,160
They'll never figure out it's me.

338
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:10,820
(The Wolf King's confidence)

339
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:11,440
What?

340
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:12,320
(Killer Zero: Jia Bing, Killer One: Hu Xianxu)
Swim on the floor?

341
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,280
(Hu Xianxu is chosen as Killer One)
For 15 seconds.

342
00:12:13,280 --> 00:12:13,680
Okay.

343
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:14,960
Don't let them see us.

344
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:15,640
We'll swim together.

345
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:17,840
How do I kill someone?

346
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,680
Cover their ears and say, "You're out".

347
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,960
(Attack method:
Cover their ears and say "You're out")

348
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:23,480
Got it.

349
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,940
(Good Guys completing tasks)
Eggies.

350
00:12:25,980 --> 00:12:27,620
(Good Guys' tasks: 1/7)
Okay.

351
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:30,020
(Good Guys' tasks: 2/7)

352
00:12:31,680 --> 00:12:32,520
Smells so good.

353
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:34,800
(Tempted to eat the props)

354
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,920
These smell amazing.

355
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:39,260
(Good Guys' tasks: 3/7)
Now I'm hungry.

356
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:40,840
Are you doing a task?

357
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:41,760
It's already done.

358
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,200
But you can peel another one.
There's five.

359
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,300
(Let's talk somewhere private)
Five of them.

360
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:49,540
(Something's up. Bai Jingting's POV)

361
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,200
Where are you going?

362
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:02,280
Bing.

363
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:03,040
(Gotcha)

364
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:03,680
Are you the Killer?

365
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,120
Hurry, infect me.

366
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:05,920
(Desperate to get hired)

367
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:06,200
What?

368
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:07,600
Recruit me.

369
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,620
(The position's already filled, bro)

370
00:13:08,660 --> 00:13:10,300
(Their secret plan's completely exposed)

371
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,120
I'll be your weapon.

372
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:16,240
(The real weapon's right here)
You're not the Killer.

373
00:13:16,240 --> 00:13:16,960
You're not Zero?

374
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:18,640
Once we peel them all, we win, right?

375
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,320
Where's the fun in that?

376
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:25,800
What are you doing?

377
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:26,840
Who does that?

378
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,760
You actually...

379
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:28,800
What's wrong with wanting

380
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:30,260
(What's wrong with wanting a job?)
to be the Killer?

381
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,040
Is it you?

382
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:33,480
Is it you?

383
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:34,520
Hurry up and infect me.

384
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,280
Infect me.

385
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,240
I wish I could.

386
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,460
(Another applicant for the job)

387
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:39,840
Who is it, then?

388
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:42,440
Bai and Song.

389
00:13:42,580 --> 00:13:44,180
(Still barking up the wrong tree)

390
00:13:44,220 --> 00:13:47,020
(Churan's got him in her sights)
These quail eggs are so hard to peel.

391
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,660
(He's actually doing the task)

392
00:13:56,240 --> 00:13:57,960
Then it must be Bai.

393
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:00,140
(No luck getting hired)

394
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,680
I'll go back and do my task.

395
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:04,500
(Wang Churan)

396
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:09,520
She ran off?

397
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,600
(She ran off? Could it be...)

398
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,320
Killer, infect me.

399
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:14,760
Infect me.

400
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:19,900
(What's going on?)

401
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,320
Infect me.

402
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,380
(A job-hunting movie)

403
00:14:22,420 --> 00:14:23,440
(A horror movie)

404
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,160
Don't kill me.

405
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:25,440
What's wrong?

406
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,840
I'm scared Bai will chase me.

407
00:14:29,280 --> 00:14:31,160
I've uncovered a huge secret.

408
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:32,960
Sound the alarm.

409
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,200
I'm sounding the alarm.

410
00:14:34,340 --> 00:14:35,440
(Sounding the alarm
before anything's happened?)

411
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:36,120
Let's check it out.

412
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:37,560
Sound the alarm.

413
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:40,360
What happened?

414
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:44,940
(That was awkward)

415
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:46,620
(Nobody saw that, right?)

416
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:48,060
(Take two)
What happened?

417
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:50,660
(Trying to recover
from the embarrassment)

418
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:51,440
Sound the alarm.

419
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:51,880
What's wrong?

420
00:14:55,360 --> 00:14:55,640
The gong.

421
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,240
What happened?

422
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,000
Where's the gong?

423
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:57,880
It's right here.

424
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:58,500
(Shen Teng's POV)

425
00:14:58,760 --> 00:15:00,400
The mallet's on that pillar behind you.

426
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,480
Don't sound the alarm.

427
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,280
It's not me.

428
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:02,800
I'm sounding the alarm.

429
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:04,980
(Ringing the gong triggers
a meeting to vote someone out)

430
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:05,800
Sound the alarm?

431
00:15:07,600 --> 00:15:08,440
Who rang it?

432
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,000
Who sounded the alarm?

433
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:14,560
If I'd waited any longer, I'd be dead.

434
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,480
Don't you dare

435
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:18,080
try to frame me.

436
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:18,740
(Something smells fishy)

437
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:20,760
(First group meeting)
Churan, you sounded the alarm. You go first.

438
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:22,640
I've uncovered a huge secret.

439
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:24,800
I was at my starting point earlier.

440
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:25,560
I was upstairs.

441
00:15:25,560 --> 00:15:27,120
Then I happened to look down.

442
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:28,960
And I saw

443
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:30,880
two people whispering to each other.

444
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:31,200
Who?

445
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:34,600
Song and Bai.

446
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:35,440
No.

447
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,120
Come back.

448
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,040
Come back, Bai.

449
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:41,440
Come back.

450
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,520
(What's wrong with looking for work?)

451
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:43,520
Bai, home is far away.

452
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:44,520
You can't walk home from here.

453
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,400
Storming out in anger.

454
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,600
I'm taking a cab home.

455
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,200
No.

456
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,040
They

457
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:51,840
were down there

458
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,640
making some weird gestures.

459
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:55,680
No.

460
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,360
What gestures?

461
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:56,640
They were...

462
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:57,200
You saw it wrong.

463
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,760
They were doing this.

464
00:16:01,880 --> 00:16:02,880
Like a bear shaking its fur?

465
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:03,920
I was teasing him.

466
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:04,960
Just messing with Bai.

467
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,840
We've been doing that since yesterday.

468
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,760
Then I went downstairs.

469
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:10,760
And Song was there,

470
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,200
peeling eggs really slowly.

471
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,560
Wait, so you sounded the alarm

472
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,920
to vote out who exactly?

473
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,680
Churan, you've gathered two more

474
00:16:17,680 --> 00:16:18,760
completely useless clues

475
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:19,800
and dragged us all here.

476
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:22,320
We had to walk pretty far.

477
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:24,760
We're all exhausted.

478
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:25,480
Seriously.

479
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:27,640
I literally climbed
over a building to get here.

480
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:28,920
Bing was way up on that hill.

481
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:29,760
You rang the gong,

482
00:16:29,760 --> 00:16:30,680
and he had to come all the way back.

483
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:31,840
If you just wanted

484
00:16:31,840 --> 00:16:33,080
to chat with us,

485
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,280
you could've said so.

486
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,640
We could've sat down at dinner

487
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:37,560
and had a nice long chat.

488
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:39,160
Think twice before ringing it again.

489
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,240
Look how out of shape I am.

490
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,240
Then Bai

491
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,560
started running at me, so I panicked.

492
00:16:44,560 --> 00:16:45,160
I sounded the alarm.

493
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:46,360
I didn't want him getting close.

494
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:48,080
Why do you keep running at people?

495
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:50,460
(Where do I even start?)

496
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,800
Same excuse as before, Bai.

497
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:52,960
He's just excited about his birthday.

498
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:53,760
Today, he's...

499
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,720
He's letting loose a little, you know?

500
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:59,760
I wanted to catch the murder in action,

501
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:01,480
but Song just wouldn't kill anyone.

502
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:04,200
Song just wouldn't kill anyone?

503
00:17:04,830 --> 00:17:06,590
Wasn't I your suspect a second ago?

504
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,760
You're acting pretty suspicious, Churan.

505
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:11,880
Wait.

506
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,110
Churan, I've gotta say,

507
00:17:13,110 --> 00:17:14,560
you're really good

508
00:17:14,560 --> 00:17:16,000
at changing the subject.

509
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,720
She realized accusing Bai
wasn't working.

510
00:17:18,640 --> 00:17:19,920
And it's his birthday.

511
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:22,720
You should write essays, Churan.

512
00:17:23,310 --> 00:17:25,280
You're all over the place.

513
00:17:26,830 --> 00:17:28,200
Can we skip voting this round?

514
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:28,840
No.

515
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,160
Churan really didn't know

516
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,790
(Playing nice to hide his identity)
we had to vote after sounding the alarm.

517
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:32,800
I didn't know either.

518
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:33,880
Wasn't she...

519
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:35,200
Wasn't she just terrified?

520
00:17:35,640 --> 00:17:36,280
And I was not?

521
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,120
You two sneak up on me,

522
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:38,560
and I shouldn't be scared?

523
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,080
Scared of what?

524
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:40,720
What could we possibly do to you?

525
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,720
Even a couple of mean words would hurt.

526
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,340
(Tough guy, soft heart)

527
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:46,240
I think

528
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:48,640
Hu's acting a little weird too.

529
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:51,620
(Loving this)

530
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:52,640
(Enjoying the Good Guys
accusing each other)

531
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:54,200
Because Hu keeps

532
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,320
defending Bai for no reason.

533
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:56,600
Churan.

534
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:58,140
(What now?)

535
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,320
If we're talking about defending people,

536
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:01,000
just now,

537
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:04,560
I only defended you.

538
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,400
I asked if we could skip voting

539
00:18:07,400 --> 00:18:09,160
because you didn't know the rules.

540
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:11,720
And now you insist on voting me out.

541
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:17,320
But Bai's been running around
since the start.

542
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,360
Because I'm desperate to get infected.

543
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,320
After how badly I played last night,

544
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:24,160
(Someone who knows exactly how he feels)
I need a chance to redeem myself.

545
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:26,040
Especially on his birthday.

546
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,840
I was alone with Jingyu.

547
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:30,440
Jingyu really wanted me
to be the Killer.

548
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,760
I practically begged him
to make a move.

549
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,820
(Jingyu wants redemption too)

550
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:34,920
But being alone with Jingyu

551
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:35,680
doesn't prove

552
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:36,800
you're not Killer Zero.

553
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,720
After what happened last night,

554
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,640
I doubt you'd recruit him again

555
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:42,840
as your partner.

556
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,360
We both need

557
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,480
a chance to redeem ourselves.

558
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,480
Maybe they each need
to prove themselves.

559
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,080
At 3AM,

560
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:55,200
I still had Bing in my head,

561
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,000
coolly shooting everyone.

562
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:58,120
(Take notes)

563
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:00,160
I just want to make up for it today.

564
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,520
Maybe there's a twist.

565
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:02,120
A twist?

566
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:03,480
There's a twist.

567
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:06,040
Okay, everyone decide who to vote for.

568
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,960
It's my first day being 33.

569
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:09,440
I don't...

570
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,800
I don't wanna clock out this early.

571
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:12,560
No way.

572
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,520
On his first day at 33,

573
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:15,920
Bai deserves a great birthday.

574
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:16,360
Vote for me.

575
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:18,220
(That came out of nowhere)

576
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:18,880
Agreed.

577
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:23,680
Seriously?

578
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:24,720
Okay, three.

579
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:25,960
Two.

580
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:27,200
One.

581
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:28,500
(Wang Churan reluctantly votes for herself)
Vote now.

582
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,020
(Wang Churan: 5 votes,
Abstentions: 3, Wang Churan out)

583
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:31,960
You all actually voted for me?

584
00:19:32,320 --> 00:19:34,020
(They really didn't hold back)
I thought I'd be the only one.

585
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:34,480
Churan,

586
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:36,360
the one who sounded the alarm

587
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,520
gets eliminated.

588
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:38,520
The mission continues.

589
00:19:39,840 --> 00:19:40,440
Come on.

590
00:19:40,440 --> 00:19:42,080
I'm gonna follow Bai around

591
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:44,000
and see how he kills people.

592
00:19:44,190 --> 00:19:45,400
You seriously

593
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:47,000
still think it's me?

594
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:49,400
Back to the starting point.

595
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,160
I didn't see that coming.

596
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:52,400
(Getting voted out
after calling the meeting)

597
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:52,960
Because earlier,

598
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:54,360
I was just being polite

599
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,440
when I said to vote me out.

600
00:19:56,660 --> 00:19:58,180
(Who said we were being polite?)

601
00:19:58,380 --> 00:19:58,900
(Jia Bing, Hu Xianxu, Shen Teng)

602
00:19:58,900 --> 00:19:59,960
Mission starts.

603
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:00,380
(Huang Jingyu, Song Yaxuan,
Bai Jingting, Fan Chengcheng)

604
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:02,700
(Rushing off to meet up)

605
00:20:04,720 --> 00:20:05,120
Come on.

606
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:07,220
(Swim on dry land for 15 seconds
to unlock Killer One's attack)

607
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,000
We need a room.

608
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,560
Once we're done, I'll just lie low.

609
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:12,320
No killing yet.

610
00:20:12,320 --> 00:20:13,920
Not until we rejoin everyone.

611
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:14,400
Yeah.

612
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,200
(Strategy: Lie low)

613
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,680
Okay, right here.

614
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,840
Come on, quick.

615
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,080
(Couldn't they do this with some dignity?)
Thirteen, fourteen, fifteen. Done.

616
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:29,620
(Ammo loaded)
Okay, let's go.

617
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,880
Let's split up for now.

618
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,880
If I wait here,
will that person show up?

619
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:37,300
(Song has arrived)

620
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:39,680
It's not me.

621
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:40,840
But if you're Zero,

622
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,920
then just

623
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:42,360
get me.

624
00:20:44,120 --> 00:20:44,800
Are you?

625
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,160
I wish I were that lucky.

626
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,320
(Poor Bai.
Maybe in another life)

627
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,040
Seriously.

628
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:52,160
What a waste of 30 seconds.

629
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,560
I got my hopes up.

630
00:20:53,560 --> 00:20:55,080
You don't have any special role.

631
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,520
I got my hopes up too.

632
00:20:58,140 --> 00:21:00,420
(Target spotted ahead)

633
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:01,600
(Bai Jingting's POV)
Bing, you alive?

634
00:21:01,600 --> 00:21:02,040
I'm alive.

635
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:06,000
Why do you keep rushing up to people?

636
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:07,080
I just came to check.

637
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:09,800
Churan's suspicions aren't unfounded.

638
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:11,560
If you're the Killer, infect him, not me.

639
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,760
(Wolf King puts on a show)
You keep running over here. It's scary.

640
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:15,720
(Bai Jingting's POV)
Who on earth is it?

641
00:21:16,860 --> 00:21:19,420
(The answer's right under your nose)

642
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:25,860
(What impressive hang time)

643
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,000
My arm's a little stiff.

644
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:41,440
This guy will try anything.

645
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:46,920
infect me, please.

646
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:47,720
It's not me.

647
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:48,480
I'm begging you.

648
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:48,880
It's not me.

649
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,480
Chengcheng.

650
00:21:49,560 --> 00:21:50,400
Point anyone and I'll kill them.

651
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:51,080
I'll go right now.

652
00:21:52,380 --> 00:21:53,620
(Since you asked so sincerely...)

653
00:21:55,980 --> 00:21:58,460
(Instantly plays along)

654
00:21:58,500 --> 00:22:00,060
(Keeping a straight face)

655
00:22:01,190 --> 00:22:03,500
Do as I do.

656
00:22:03,690 --> 00:22:06,160
I'll do as you do.

657
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:08,280
- You need to raise it higher.
- Do as I do.

658
00:22:08,580 --> 00:22:10,480
I'll do as you do.

659
00:22:10,480 --> 00:22:10,890
Go on.

660
00:22:10,890 --> 00:22:11,250
Okay.

661
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,360
Kill Hu.

662
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:14,500
(Committed to the act)

663
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,880
Why does that feel so unconvincing?

664
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,000
That...

665
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:19,170
(Just a hunch)
"Infection" gesture.

666
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:20,120
What's my command to kill him?

667
00:22:20,120 --> 00:22:21,360
Just do this to him.

668
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:22,040
Do what?

669
00:22:22,040 --> 00:22:22,440
This.

670
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:25,840
Seriously?

671
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,400
Why don't I feel

672
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,160
any sense of responsibility right now?

673
00:22:30,020 --> 00:22:32,580
(The responsible real killer)
These quail eggs are so hard to peel.

674
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:33,200
Song.

675
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:35,000
What are you doing?

676
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:35,600
Peeling eggs.

677
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,400
You got one?

678
00:22:37,400 --> 00:22:37,760
Yeah.

679
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:44,800
What for?

680
00:22:46,820 --> 00:22:49,580
(Song Yaxuan's POV)

681
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:50,280
Hurry up.

682
00:22:51,420 --> 00:22:53,100
(Hu Xianxu's POV)
A bodycam?

683
00:22:53,240 --> 00:22:54,640
(Attack method)
Cover his ears and say "You're out".

684
00:22:55,020 --> 00:22:56,620
(Ready to strike)

685
00:22:59,580 --> 00:23:01,300
(All that confidence, gone)

686
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:02,280
(Keeping up appearances)

687
00:23:02,280 --> 00:23:03,360
Whose room is this?

688
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:05,840
Something's going on in that room.

689
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:07,560
Several people went in.

690
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:07,840
Let's go.

691
00:23:07,840 --> 00:23:08,640
They still haven't come out.

692
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:11,560
(Someone's approaching. Attack on hold)

693
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,440
Are you Killer Zero?

694
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:16,680
(Pretending to help to be more credible)
You're making this so complicated.

695
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:17,280
It's just us two.

696
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:19,120
I'm not.

697
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:20,720
Then get out.

698
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:23,600
(Saving half for later)

699
00:23:23,600 --> 00:23:24,200
Let's go.

700
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:26,520
I haven't finished peeling mine.

701
00:23:26,520 --> 00:23:27,500
(Only one quail egg per task station)
You only need to peel one.

702
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,040
Don't ruin mine.

703
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:36,400
What?

704
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:38,440
Someone's blocking the view.

705
00:23:39,040 --> 00:23:40,000
They're trying to kill us.

706
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:42,160
We're peeling eggs.

707
00:23:42,720 --> 00:23:43,800
Are you trying to sabotage us?

708
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:44,400
I want to see.

709
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:46,280
They're out.

710
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:47,320
Let me try.

711
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:49,080
Go ahead.

712
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:52,120
What?

713
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:52,880
I'll try it.

714
00:23:52,880 --> 00:23:53,560
See if it's real.

715
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:54,120
See if it works.

716
00:23:57,320 --> 00:23:57,880
What are you doing?

717
00:23:58,560 --> 00:24:00,000
You're doing it wrong. Like this.

718
00:24:04,960 --> 00:24:05,680
Is he dead yet?

719
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,560
Just tell me
who was responsible yesterday.

720
00:24:10,140 --> 00:24:11,580
(Confused)

721
00:24:11,620 --> 00:24:18,060
(Hehehehe)

722
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:20,400
You big idiot.

723
00:24:23,940 --> 00:24:25,540
(Checking the results)

724
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:29,320
What's wrong?

725
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:31,760
What?

726
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:33,080
Those two are the bad guys.

727
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:33,640
Who's the bad guy?

728
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:34,480
I'm not a bad guy.

729
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:36,880
Those two are.

730
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:37,680
Which two?

731
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,240
They spent a whole round in that room

732
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,640
and couldn't peel a single egg.

733
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:41,960
Ask Song.

734
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:43,200
These are really hard to peel.

735
00:24:43,840 --> 00:24:44,960
These eggs are seriously hard to peel.

736
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:45,600
I've peeled one before.

737
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:46,960
Why's it suddenly easy now?

738
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,360
Run. Don't let him kill us.

739
00:24:51,360 --> 00:24:52,440
Clear the way.

740
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:54,950
(Confident in his false conclusion)
Clear the way.

741
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:55,320
This guy...

742
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:56,960
He's spreading rumors.

743
00:24:57,960 --> 00:24:59,240
Do you have to walk around

744
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:00,120
with your belly sticking out?

745
00:25:00,620 --> 00:25:03,620
(Shen Teng's POV)

746
00:25:03,620 --> 00:25:04,980
(Quick to take the hint)

747
00:25:08,980 --> 00:25:10,820
(That was pretty loud)

748
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:12,160
What's with him? What did he do?

749
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:12,760
No idea.

750
00:25:13,680 --> 00:25:14,560
Guys, take a seat.

751
00:25:15,260 --> 00:25:16,920
(Second group meeting)

752
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,920
Song.

753
00:25:21,440 --> 00:25:22,680
And Hu.

754
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:24,840
One of them is Killer Zero,

755
00:25:24,840 --> 00:25:26,640
and the other's the Killer One.

756
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:28,520
They spent five minutes in there

757
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:29,640
and couldn't peel a single egg.

758
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:30,960
It wasn't five minutes.

759
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:31,440
Suspicious, right?

760
00:25:31,440 --> 00:25:32,200
It wasn't five minutes.

761
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,000
Three minutes.

762
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,720
Could you peel that egg if you tried?

763
00:25:34,740 --> 00:25:36,100
No.

764
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:37,800
(Speechless)
You really can't.

765
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:38,120
See?

766
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:40,000
Now they're arguing.

767
00:25:41,460 --> 00:25:43,060
(Wrongfully accused)

768
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,080
It's those two.

769
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:45,240
Okay, who are we voting for?

770
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:46,140
(Ready for the order)

771
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:46,760
Hu Xianxu.

772
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:51,840
He was wasting my time.

773
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:53,520
I'm telling you,

774
00:25:53,520 --> 00:25:54,840
I just thought he was too slow.

775
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:55,880
I peeled mine in no time.

776
00:25:55,880 --> 00:25:57,520
It's not about who's fast or slow.

777
00:25:57,520 --> 00:25:58,600
You ate half and left half.

778
00:25:58,600 --> 00:25:59,480
How does that count?

779
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:00,840
Let's vote Hu first.

780
00:26:00,980 --> 00:26:02,260
(Killer in danger)

781
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:03,600
I think Teng might have

782
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:04,800
(Playing it cool)
figured out the rules.

783
00:26:04,800 --> 00:26:06,080
(He's not wrong)
Exactly.

784
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:08,040
If he's the wolf, he won't kill anyone.

785
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:09,200
He'll just sound the alarm.

786
00:26:10,180 --> 00:26:12,860
(You're accusing me?)

787
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:14,240
You're giving me too much credit.

788
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:15,440
He's figured out the rules.

789
00:26:15,440 --> 00:26:16,480
I wouldn't kill anyone.

790
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:17,480
I'd just sound the alarm

791
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:19,000
and accuse someone.

792
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:20,840
You'd have to vote someone out, right?

793
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:21,800
Makes sense.

794
00:26:22,060 --> 00:26:23,360
(That's actually convincing)

795
00:26:23,360 --> 00:26:24,480
Why don't we try voting Teng out?

796
00:26:26,640 --> 00:26:27,640
You never leave the room anyway.

797
00:26:30,320 --> 00:26:31,520
It's definitely Teng.

798
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:32,720
(Still misleading the Good Guys)
Aren't you just stirring things up?

799
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:33,040
Come on.

800
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:35,000
Let's try voting Teng out.

801
00:26:35,520 --> 00:26:36,640
Just for fun.

802
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:38,320
See what happens.

803
00:26:38,320 --> 00:26:40,720
Jingyu sees the best in everyone.

804
00:26:42,560 --> 00:26:43,480
Teng

805
00:26:43,480 --> 00:26:44,840
is about to lose it.

806
00:26:44,840 --> 00:26:45,640
Teng's about to lose it.

807
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:46,960
You really want to film for three days

808
00:26:46,960 --> 00:26:48,520
and embarrass yourself every day?

809
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:53,240
I've been...

810
00:26:53,240 --> 00:26:54,280
(Speaking up for himself)

811
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:55,480
I've had an egg every round.

812
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:56,560
Let's vote.

813
00:26:56,560 --> 00:26:57,340
(Not listening at all)
Let's vote you out and see.

814
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:01,320
No.

815
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:02,140
(A rather weak protest)

816
00:27:04,920 --> 00:27:06,640
Now I kind of want to vote for him.

817
00:27:07,140 --> 00:27:08,660
(You too?)

818
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:10,400
No.

819
00:27:10,920 --> 00:27:11,720
(Won't take no for an answer)
I'm doing it anyway.

820
00:27:11,980 --> 00:27:13,660
(How did it come to this?)

821
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:14,320
Time to vote.

822
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:15,920
I vote for Teng.

823
00:27:16,060 --> 00:27:17,340
(You accuse me, I accuse you)

824
00:27:17,400 --> 00:27:18,320
Let's try it.

825
00:27:18,320 --> 00:27:19,960
Voting for Number Five
would be embarrassing.

826
00:27:20,180 --> 00:27:21,140
(How embarrassing)

827
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:22,640
Wouldn't that embarrass us too?

828
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:24,280
I'm fine with embarrassing myself.

829
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:28,560
You little brats.

830
00:27:30,360 --> 00:27:30,760
Come on.

831
00:27:31,120 --> 00:27:31,680
Please vote.

832
00:27:31,860 --> 00:27:33,140
(Shen Teng*5, Abstain*1,
Hu Xianxu*1, Shen Teng out)

833
00:27:33,280 --> 00:27:34,160
What?!

834
00:27:34,760 --> 00:27:36,920
Teng got voted out by a landslide.

835
00:27:37,020 --> 00:27:38,340
(The only one who abstained)

836
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:39,800
He's furious.

837
00:27:40,680 --> 00:27:42,120
No, I was afraid we'd vote out the wolf.

838
00:27:44,220 --> 00:27:45,360
(Don't worry. I'm not going anywhere)
This round

839
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:47,040
had me so stressed.

840
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:48,680
We won, right?

841
00:27:48,680 --> 00:27:49,720
Game over.

842
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:51,080
Mission continues.

843
00:27:51,080 --> 00:27:51,880
Continues?

844
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:52,840
Did we vote wrongly?

845
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,600
Everyone,
return to your starting points.

846
00:27:58,080 --> 00:27:59,360
This Killer Zero is really clever.

847
00:28:00,280 --> 00:28:01,880
He causes chaos
without lifting a finger.

848
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:04,360
Is he clever,

849
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:06,960
or are some people just clueless?

850
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:09,320
Clueless.

851
00:28:12,200 --> 00:28:13,400
Where are you going, Teng?

852
00:28:13,400 --> 00:28:15,080
He's like strutting down a slope,

853
00:28:15,080 --> 00:28:15,840
looking

854
00:28:15,840 --> 00:28:17,280
all confident.

855
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:18,520
Even about shout "clear the way"!

856
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:21,920
Who threw this paper here?

857
00:28:22,100 --> 00:28:23,380
(He's even kicking paper on the ground)

858
00:28:24,280 --> 00:28:25,680
He's got nowhere to vent his anger.

859
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:27,960
Hurry up and find the eggs.

860
00:28:30,320 --> 00:28:31,220
(Hu Xianxu, Jia Bing, Song Yaxuan)
Mission begins.

861
00:28:31,220 --> 00:28:31,940
(Bai Jingting,
Huang Jingyu, Fan Chengcheng)

862
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:33,280
I'll go find Jingyu.

863
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:36,160
If we pull this off,

864
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:37,160
it'll be our highlight moment.

865
00:28:38,160 --> 00:28:39,320
If we fail, it's his fault.

866
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:41,320
I want

867
00:28:41,320 --> 00:28:42,400
to stay outside. It's safer.

868
00:28:43,020 --> 00:28:43,680
(Safest in plain sight)

869
00:28:43,680 --> 00:28:46,480
Are you the gun or Killer Zero?

870
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:47,560
I'm a Good Guy.

871
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:48,600
He's the gun.

872
00:28:48,600 --> 00:28:50,120
I'm not. I'm neither.

873
00:28:58,840 --> 00:28:59,680
Hey, weren't you scared?

874
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:01,760
She risked her life to save you.

875
00:29:01,760 --> 00:29:02,720
What do you mean, wasn't she scared?

876
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,920
She's terrified of bugs the most.

877
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:06,520
You owe her your life.

878
00:29:07,040 --> 00:29:07,600
Got it.

879
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:08,600
Don't feel too pressured, though.

880
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:09,400
It's not like he can repay you.

881
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:13,320
If you hadn't brought it up,

882
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:14,650
I'd have forgotten about it.

883
00:29:17,560 --> 00:29:18,520
If it's Jingyu,

884
00:29:18,520 --> 00:29:19,920
then he's working with Hu.

885
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:21,920
He voted for you to protect Hu.

886
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,280
Chengcheng's just a complete idiot.

887
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,620
(Look who's talking)

888
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:26,840
Where's Bing?

889
00:29:26,840 --> 00:29:29,120
I haven't seen him at all.

890
00:29:36,200 --> 00:29:37,080
Let's just watch them play.

891
00:29:37,340 --> 00:29:39,020
(The calm of someone
who knows everything)

892
00:29:39,060 --> 00:29:41,340
(Ready to make a move)

893
00:29:46,440 --> 00:29:47,000
Chengcheng.

894
00:29:52,700 --> 00:29:54,460
(A wild "whale" appears)

895
00:29:57,880 --> 00:29:59,280
You scared me.

896
00:30:00,220 --> 00:30:02,060
(Rushing over after hearing the noise)

897
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:04,460
(Too many people. Can't strike)

898
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,240
I'm Killer Zero.

899
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,240
I'm infecting you now.

900
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:24,960
Infect me.

901
00:30:25,600 --> 00:30:26,080
No, wait.

902
00:30:28,480 --> 00:30:30,440
Why don't we set a trap?

903
00:30:30,780 --> 00:30:32,820
(A trap?)

904
00:30:34,160 --> 00:30:36,320
Go wait for me in a room farther away.

905
00:30:36,320 --> 00:30:37,120
I'll give you a task.

906
00:30:38,620 --> 00:30:40,740
(Can barely hide his grin)

907
00:30:48,620 --> 00:30:50,460
(Nothing beats having a job to do)

908
00:30:55,280 --> 00:30:56,040
Where are they?

909
00:30:58,480 --> 00:30:59,920
What are you two doing?

910
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:01,520
Why does this room
have so many entrances?

911
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:03,200
I was just talking to him,
and somehow we ended up in here.

912
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:05,880
This bathroom isn't very private.

913
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:07,000
People can come in from both sides.

914
00:31:07,300 --> 00:31:08,520
(Back to plotting)

915
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:10,240
Don't these places have second floors?

916
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,840
One of us can hide upstairs

917
00:31:11,840 --> 00:31:12,560
and keep watch.

918
00:31:13,280 --> 00:31:14,800
The other pretends he's alone

919
00:31:14,800 --> 00:31:15,840
to see who comes to attack.

920
00:31:15,840 --> 00:31:16,960
What if nobody comes?

921
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:20,160
But what if someone does?

922
00:31:20,160 --> 00:31:20,800
(Purely relying on luck)

923
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:21,800
It'll be our highlight moment.

924
00:31:21,800 --> 00:31:23,740
(A highlight moment in the making)
Who do you think will show up?

925
00:31:23,760 --> 00:31:25,200
Why don't we stay here?

926
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,960
One of us can find

927
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:27,640
a hiding spot

928
00:31:27,640 --> 00:31:28,560
and secretly watch.

929
00:31:36,300 --> 00:31:38,500
(Waiting for their big moment)

930
00:31:39,040 --> 00:31:39,520
Where's Chengcheng?

931
00:31:40,180 --> 00:31:42,180
(Waiting patiently)

932
00:31:48,640 --> 00:31:49,200
Peeling eggs.

933
00:31:50,660 --> 00:31:53,260
(Waiting for a job to come his way)

934
00:31:56,620 --> 00:31:58,900
(Coast is clear)

935
00:31:58,980 --> 00:32:00,500
(So excited. Can't wait)

936
00:32:02,760 --> 00:32:03,920
You're eliminated.

937
00:32:09,460 --> 00:32:11,980
(What an emotional roller coaster)

938
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:18,960
At least you killed me
somewhere comfortable.

939
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:21,180
(Just forcing a smile)

940
00:32:21,220 --> 00:32:23,860
(Fan Chengcheng out)

941
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:26,340
(Still waiting for their big moment)

942
00:32:27,280 --> 00:32:28,000
Killer.

943
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:30,600
Hey, Killer.

944
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:33,520
There's no action yet?

945
00:32:34,380 --> 00:32:35,320
Is Chengcheng...

946
00:32:35,320 --> 00:32:36,040
(Almost gave himself away)
No.

947
00:32:36,040 --> 00:32:37,240
Is Bai dead?

948
00:32:37,240 --> 00:32:37,720
No.

949
00:32:38,240 --> 00:32:39,040
I'm going to check on him.

950
00:32:40,240 --> 00:32:41,520
Did you kill Bai?

951
00:32:41,520 --> 00:32:42,360
I'm telling you, I didn't.

952
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:43,760
Then why do you need to check?

953
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:46,040
Why won't you let me check?

954
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:47,000
I'm telling you, he's not dead.

955
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Then why check?

956
00:32:54,600 --> 00:32:56,000
Both of you go check.

957
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:57,040
What do I have to check?

958
00:32:57,040 --> 00:32:57,920
If he were dead, I'd tell you.

959
00:32:58,920 --> 00:33:00,320
If he goes in there and kills...

960
00:33:01,120 --> 00:33:02,160
And frames me for it?

961
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:02,400
Yes.

962
00:33:03,840 --> 00:33:04,840
Hu.

963
00:33:09,440 --> 00:33:10,520
That idiot.

964
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:12,400
I seriously can't believe him.

965
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,480
Huang Jingyu.

966
00:33:14,080 --> 00:33:14,800
Where's Bai?

967
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:16,120
Buried.

968
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:17,440
He's already buried by now.

969
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:20,480
Bai.

970
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:22,480
Where's Bai?

971
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:30,160
You scared me to death.

972
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:31,680
What are you doing?

973
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:33,800
You're eliminated.

974
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:35,400
Sound the alarm!

975
00:33:35,680 --> 00:33:38,360
Sound the alarm!

976
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:39,480
Sound the alarm!

977
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:40,480
Sound the alarm!

978
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:42,640
Sound the alarm!

979
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,000
Bai's gone.

980
00:33:45,560 --> 00:33:46,680
Sound the alarm.

981
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:48,600
We're done for.

982
00:33:48,600 --> 00:33:50,600
The Good Guys have already lost.

983
00:33:51,480 --> 00:33:52,600
Sound the alarm.

984
00:33:53,060 --> 00:33:54,900
(Okay. Aah)

985
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,680
Huang Jingyu killed Bai.

986
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:57,880
He hid him

987
00:33:57,880 --> 00:33:58,680
inside that little cabinet.

988
00:33:59,000 --> 00:33:59,760
Happy birthday.

989
00:34:00,200 --> 00:34:00,800
Sorry.

990
00:34:00,800 --> 00:34:01,580
(So you weren't the Killer)

991
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:02,800
Where's Chengcheng?

992
00:34:06,840 --> 00:34:07,680
Chengcheng's gone?

993
00:34:08,080 --> 00:34:09,150
Ring the gong.

994
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,800
I saw Jingyu

995
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:18,440
had already buried Bai.

996
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:19,800
He hid him inside that little cabinet.

997
00:34:20,630 --> 00:34:22,300
(Mr. Huang arrives to solve the case)
So what happened just now?

998
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:23,560
Bai and I planned

999
00:34:24,190 --> 00:34:25,960
for one of us to be bait
while the other lay in ambush

1000
00:34:25,960 --> 00:34:27,520
to see who the Killer would target.

1001
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:29,920
Then I came out,

1002
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:31,520
and Hu wanted to go in and check.

1003
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:33,400
He searched everywhere
but couldn't find Bai.

1004
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:34,320
Then Teng reminded me,

1005
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:35,320
what if he killed someone

1006
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:36,840
and framed me for it?

1007
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:37,880
I thought he was right.

1008
00:34:37,880 --> 00:34:39,040
So I rushed back in.

1009
00:34:39,040 --> 00:34:40,520
Then Hu found Bai,

1010
00:34:40,520 --> 00:34:41,280
killed him,

1011
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:42,150
and started shouting.

1012
00:34:42,630 --> 00:34:43,280
But it's fine.

1013
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:44,320
You're safe. We won't vote for you.

1014
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:45,440
There's no point voting for you.

1015
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:46,520
We need to find Killer Zero.

1016
00:34:47,230 --> 00:34:47,840
So now,

1017
00:34:47,840 --> 00:34:49,840
(The clearest deduction yet)
Churan and Teng are both out.

1018
00:34:49,840 --> 00:34:51,190
I thought Chengcheng was Killer Zero,

1019
00:34:51,190 --> 00:34:52,190
but he's out too.

1020
00:34:52,800 --> 00:34:53,360
That leaves

1021
00:34:53,360 --> 00:34:53,800
Song,

1022
00:34:53,800 --> 00:34:54,350
(Remaining players:)
me and Hu.

1023
00:34:54,350 --> 00:34:55,360
(Killer Zero, Good Guy, Good Guy, Killer One)
me and Hu.

1024
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:57,280
I can't outvote those two.

1025
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:00,120
What?

1026
00:35:00,880 --> 00:35:01,920
When you do the math...

1027
00:35:02,640 --> 00:35:03,440
I can't outvote them.

1028
00:35:03,440 --> 00:35:04,640
Even if I vote, I'll lose.

1029
00:35:05,960 --> 00:35:06,680
Come on.

1030
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:08,280
Hu, will you vote
for Killer Zero with me?

1031
00:35:10,520 --> 00:35:11,280
The number of Killers

1032
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:13,160
equals the number
of remaining Good Guys.

1033
00:35:13,160 --> 00:35:14,120
The Killers win.

1034
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:18,680
Wasn't my intuition

1035
00:35:18,680 --> 00:35:20,000
a one-in-three chance?

1036
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:21,240
It's pretty accurate after all.

1037
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:22,360
Just now you picked

1038
00:35:22,360 --> 00:35:23,640
picked five people, didn't you?

1039
00:35:23,640 --> 00:35:24,880
I picked Hu.

1040
00:35:25,320 --> 00:35:26,280
The key is

1041
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:27,760
knowing how to use people.

1042
00:35:27,820 --> 00:35:29,660
(The Wolf King's recruitment strategy)

1043
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:31,720
I originally considered Jingting,

1044
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:33,880
but today's a special day for him.

1045
00:35:33,880 --> 00:35:34,960
Using him would've exposed me.

1046
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:37,000
He's been very aggressive today.

1047
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:39,600
I considered Jingyu too.

1048
00:35:40,080 --> 00:35:41,760
We worked well together yesterday.

1049
00:35:41,760 --> 00:35:43,040
But in the second half
of yesterday's game,

1050
00:35:43,040 --> 00:35:44,120
I saw his teamwork with Bai,

1051
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:45,080
and to be frank,

1052
00:35:45,080 --> 00:35:46,480
I was a little disappointed.

1053
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:48,640
So I thought I'd choose someone

1054
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:50,280
with the most consistent performance.

1055
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:50,960
That's why I picked Hu.

1056
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:52,000
Impressive.

1057
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:54,040
Did you take extra classes
over the summer?

1058
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,480
"Werewolf Summer Camp".

1059
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:02,880
What were you plotting with Chengcheng?

1060
00:36:02,880 --> 00:36:03,600
I tricked Chengcheng.

1061
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:04,960
I told him I was Killer Zero

1062
00:36:04,960 --> 00:36:05,960
and wanted to infect him.

1063
00:36:05,960 --> 00:36:07,120
Then I told him to wait in that room.

1064
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:10,160
He just nodded.

1065
00:36:15,620 --> 00:36:17,580
(Don't tell them)

1066
00:36:17,680 --> 00:36:18,840
Not only killed physically,

1067
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:20,280
but was also crushed emotionally.

1068
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,440
He got humiliated right
before his death.

1069
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:25,440
(Undercover Werewolf, Round 2. Roles Reshuffled)
Round two begins.

1070
00:36:25,440 --> 00:36:26,360
We'll distribute the roles.

1071
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:28,120
Give me a role card.

1072
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:31,560
Come infect me.

1073
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,040
Stop saying that.

1074
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:34,920
When someone actually approaches you,

1075
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:36,040
you're the first to run.

1076
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:41,120
Great.

1077
00:36:43,640 --> 00:36:44,080
I'm done playing.

1078
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:47,520
Everyone,

1079
00:36:47,520 --> 00:36:48,280
please close your eyes.

1080
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,760
Killer Zero,

1081
00:36:52,760 --> 00:36:53,400
please open your eyes.

1082
00:36:53,780 --> 00:36:54,440
(Killer Zero: Secret)

1083
00:36:54,440 --> 00:36:54,720
Okay.

1084
00:36:55,040 --> 00:36:55,600
Everyone,

1085
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:56,520
please open your eyes.

1086
00:36:57,120 --> 00:36:58,320
(Killer Zero: Secret)
Head to your starting points.

1087
00:36:58,320 --> 00:36:59,520
Round two begins.

1088
00:37:00,020 --> 00:37:01,780
(Round 2: Hu Xianxu, Jia Bing,
Shen Teng, Song Yaxuan)

1089
00:37:01,780 --> 00:37:03,540
(Huang Jingyu, Fan Chengcheng,
Bai Jingting, Wang Churan)

1090
00:37:03,620 --> 00:37:05,260
(Arriving at the starting point)

1091
00:37:09,640 --> 00:37:10,560
This one's hard to grab.

1092
00:37:10,920 --> 00:37:12,240
Mission begins.

1093
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:15,000
Let me see.

1094
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:15,760
Can you really peel an egg

1095
00:37:17,080 --> 00:37:18,080
that quickly?

1096
00:37:22,200 --> 00:37:23,360
You actually can.

1097
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:24,680
That's fast.

1098
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:25,960
Okay, one egg done.

1099
00:37:26,060 --> 00:37:27,500
(Good Guy Task Progress: 1/7)

1100
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:30,080
I'll hide here for a bit

1101
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:31,280
and see if anyone steals my egg.

1102
00:37:31,460 --> 00:37:33,100
(A brilliant ambush in progress)

1103
00:37:40,480 --> 00:37:41,000
One egg peeled.

1104
00:37:41,180 --> 00:37:43,020
(Good Guy Task Progress: 2/7)

1105
00:37:44,160 --> 00:37:45,480
What's the point of living

1106
00:37:45,480 --> 00:37:46,400
if I can't get the Killer role?

1107
00:37:46,460 --> 00:37:52,340
(Completely at peace)

1108
00:37:52,340 --> 00:37:54,100
(Good Guy Task Progress: 3/7)

1109
00:37:55,240 --> 00:37:56,000
I'll leave this here.

1110
00:37:58,160 --> 00:37:59,040
If I witness something,

1111
00:37:59,040 --> 00:38:00,440
can I record it with this?

1112
00:38:00,440 --> 00:38:02,300
(What a genius I am)

1113
00:38:02,380 --> 00:38:04,020
(Bodycam)

1114
00:38:06,060 --> 00:38:06,900
(Shen Teng)

1115
00:38:06,900 --> 00:38:09,380
(Recording started)

1116
00:38:13,400 --> 00:38:14,120
There's no egg here too.

1117
00:38:14,420 --> 00:38:16,300
(Recording)

1118
00:38:16,340 --> 00:38:18,320
(Huang Jingyu's camera POV)

1119
00:38:18,320 --> 00:38:19,240
Are you dead?

1120
00:38:19,240 --> 00:38:19,800
No.

1121
00:38:20,040 --> 00:38:21,440
Then why are you holding that?

1122
00:38:21,440 --> 00:38:22,560
I wanted to see what you were doing.

1123
00:38:23,560 --> 00:38:24,640
You've already got one there.

1124
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:25,400
Why are you taking another?

1125
00:38:26,340 --> 00:38:28,340
(Huang Jingyu's handheld camera
and chest camera)

1126
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:30,880
Do it with me.

1127
00:38:30,900 --> 00:38:32,120
(Is the Killer about to pick me?)

1128
00:38:32,120 --> 00:38:32,600
Okay.

1129
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:37,800
Kill Jia Bing.

1130
00:38:39,520 --> 00:38:40,800
Wait, it's that simple?

1131
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:43,280
Let's kill him later.

1132
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:45,240
What's the killing gesture?

1133
00:38:46,260 --> 00:38:47,620
(Mwah)

1134
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:49,640
Isn't that a bit of a stretch?

1135
00:38:49,780 --> 00:38:51,620
(Reason wins over the urge
to be a Killer)

1136
00:38:51,840 --> 00:38:53,120
I think they went that way.

1137
00:38:55,740 --> 00:38:57,340
(Suspicious person spotted)

1138
00:39:15,340 --> 00:39:18,220
(Caught in the act)
What are you looking at?

1139
00:39:28,580 --> 00:39:29,980
(Keeping a safe distance)

1140
00:39:30,060 --> 00:39:31,940
(Come here)

1141
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:33,320
You're Killer Zero, right?

1142
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:34,280
I'm infecting you.

1143
00:39:38,300 --> 00:39:39,260
(Something's suspicious about Churan)

1144
00:39:40,360 --> 00:39:41,800
Who is it, anyway?

1145
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:42,760
(Pick me)

1146
00:39:42,760 --> 00:39:43,920
I'll circle around outside

1147
00:39:43,920 --> 00:39:45,240
and check in a bit.

1148
00:39:45,700 --> 00:39:52,900
(Circling around to investigate)

1149
00:39:56,740 --> 00:39:58,660
(Bai Jingting's POV)

1150
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:01,040
I peeled an egg.

1151
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:02,800
I peeled an egg.

1152
00:40:04,400 --> 00:40:05,760
I peeled an egg in this room.

1153
00:40:06,040 --> 00:40:07,200
Let's go in and take a look together.

1154
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:08,200
Can we hold hands?

1155
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:08,720
Let's go.

1156
00:40:18,160 --> 00:40:19,040
What are you trying to do?

1157
00:40:20,580 --> 00:40:26,540
(Front door, back door)

1158
00:40:28,780 --> 00:40:31,180
(Sneaking around from behind)

1159
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:32,440
There's one on my plate.

1160
00:40:33,040 --> 00:40:33,400
I peeled it.

1161
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:34,360
It's peeled.

1162
00:40:35,380 --> 00:40:37,620
(Back-door ambush team)

1163
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:39,640
I peeled an egg over there.

1164
00:40:39,640 --> 00:40:40,500
(Front-door scouting team)

1165
00:40:41,040 --> 00:40:42,120
You scared me.

1166
00:40:42,700 --> 00:40:43,860
(Quietly recording)

1167
00:40:44,260 --> 00:40:45,160
(Huang Jingyu's camera POV)

1168
00:40:45,160 --> 00:40:46,400
Why's Jingyu gone quiet?

1169
00:40:47,560 --> 00:40:48,120
Is he dead?

1170
00:40:48,120 --> 00:40:48,520
No.

1171
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:51,880
He's just doing something pointless.

1172
00:40:51,880 --> 00:40:53,560
(Huang Jingyu's camera POV)

1173
00:40:53,560 --> 00:40:54,120
Wait.

1174
00:40:54,120 --> 00:40:55,400
Is he filming his own show now?

1175
00:40:57,560 --> 00:40:58,960
Is that it?

1176
00:40:58,960 --> 00:40:59,960
Are you livestreaming?

1177
00:40:59,960 --> 00:41:01,000
We've got a second camera crew.

1178
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:02,960
A second camera crew.

1179
00:41:02,960 --> 00:41:03,800
Alright.

1180
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:04,520
You little rascal.

1181
00:41:06,260 --> 00:41:08,580
(Still hiding like a pro)

1182
00:41:13,860 --> 00:41:14,940
(Coming out to check)

1183
00:41:14,960 --> 00:41:15,800
Did you peel an egg?

1184
00:41:16,320 --> 00:41:16,680
Yeah.

1185
00:41:16,680 --> 00:41:17,200
In that room.

1186
00:41:17,200 --> 00:41:18,280
I'll go check.

1187
00:41:18,280 --> 00:41:19,440
Don't steal my egg.

1188
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,640
I'll keep an eye on you.

1189
00:41:23,020 --> 00:41:26,140
(Teng silently follows)

1190
00:41:29,140 --> 00:41:30,700
(Hu watches closely from behind)

1191
00:41:31,380 --> 00:41:34,460
(Huang follows right behind)

1192
00:41:36,580 --> 00:41:37,740
(Teng sneaks around)

1193
00:41:38,320 --> 00:41:39,440
I peeled one. I'm not the Killer.

1194
00:41:39,800 --> 00:41:40,320
Okay.

1195
00:41:42,380 --> 00:41:43,380
(Teng watching, Hu watching)

1196
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:48,880
Shen Teng.

1197
00:41:49,080 --> 00:41:49,400
Who?

1198
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:50,000
Teng.

1199
00:41:50,640 --> 00:41:51,360
What?

1200
00:41:51,360 --> 00:41:52,240
Teng.

1201
00:42:18,680 --> 00:42:20,600
All four of you

1202
00:42:21,240 --> 00:42:22,400
know exactly where I'm going.

1203
00:42:23,680 --> 00:42:24,920
You're trying to steal an egg.

1204
00:42:25,240 --> 00:42:26,360
(Suspicious)
You're trying to steal an egg.

1205
00:42:26,420 --> 00:42:27,180
(Highly suspicious)

1206
00:42:27,480 --> 00:42:28,680
I was going to check the eggs.

1207
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:31,040
Is the egg still there?

1208
00:42:31,040 --> 00:42:31,400
Yeah.

1209
00:42:32,200 --> 00:42:33,080
He just picked it up.

1210
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:34,360
We came out too early.

1211
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:36,400
I peeled this egg.

1212
00:42:36,600 --> 00:42:37,700
How come you can peel one now?

1213
00:42:37,700 --> 00:42:39,590
(Chin attack)
How come you can peel one now?

1214
00:42:39,600 --> 00:42:40,680
You suddenly grew up?

1215
00:42:40,680 --> 00:42:42,440
I really gave my all.

1216
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,840
Look, it's all cracked.

1217
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:47,320
Teng, your mic fell off.

1218
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:48,600
It did?

1219
00:42:48,740 --> 00:42:49,400
(Going back inside
to fix his equipment)

1220
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,440
I want to adjust my mic too.

1221
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:51,760
Did mine fall off?

1222
00:42:52,080 --> 00:42:52,680
Yeah.

1223
00:42:55,080 --> 00:42:56,440
Congratulations. You're hired.

1224
00:42:57,520 --> 00:42:59,600
Killer Zero, please open your eyes.

1225
00:42:59,620 --> 00:43:00,680
(Killer Zero: Fan Chengcheng)

1226
00:43:00,680 --> 00:43:02,320
Let's infect the old man.

1227
00:43:02,640 --> 00:43:03,960
Congratulations. You're hired.

1228
00:43:04,600 --> 00:43:06,360
You're now Killer One.

1229
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:08,680
(Killer One: Shen Teng)
First, we need to shower for 15 seconds.

1230
00:43:08,680 --> 00:43:09,480
You've got a bullet.

1231
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:10,200
Come on, start showering.

1232
00:43:10,960 --> 00:43:11,600
Shower?

1233
00:43:11,600 --> 00:43:13,200
(Shower with Killer One for 15 seconds)
Come on, pretend to shower.

1234
00:43:13,200 --> 00:43:14,320
(to unlock the ability to attack)
One, two, three, four, five,

1235
00:43:14,320 --> 00:43:15,320
six, seven, eight, nine, ten,

1236
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:16,720
eleven, twelve,
thirteen, fourteen, fifteen.

1237
00:43:16,720 --> 00:43:17,880
(Killer One Shen Teng, Weapon loaded)
Your killing move

1238
00:43:17,880 --> 00:43:19,120
is to pat someone on the back

1239
00:43:19,120 --> 00:43:20,360
and say "You're out"
and they'll be dead.

1240
00:43:20,620 --> 00:43:21,240
(Attack method: Pat their back
and say "You're out")

1241
00:43:21,240 --> 00:43:22,520
Say "You're out" behind them.

1242
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:23,840
Give them a pat.

1243
00:43:23,840 --> 00:43:24,560
Whose back?

1244
00:43:24,560 --> 00:43:25,800
Anyone. You can kill whoever you want.

1245
00:43:27,020 --> 00:43:28,580
(Sudden intrusion)

1246
00:43:28,660 --> 00:43:30,460
(Aah)

1247
00:43:33,300 --> 00:43:35,740
(Sits down awkwardly)

1248
00:43:37,820 --> 00:43:38,520
(Staring intensely)

1249
00:43:38,520 --> 00:43:39,000
What?

1250
00:43:40,380 --> 00:43:42,580
(Already has a peeled egg)

1251
00:43:44,900 --> 00:43:47,260
(Song secretly observes)

1252
00:43:47,340 --> 00:43:48,640
(Witness +1)

1253
00:43:48,640 --> 00:43:49,280
What's he doing?

1254
00:43:50,860 --> 00:43:53,140
(Caught from both sides)

1255
00:43:54,020 --> 00:43:55,140
(Looking guilty)

1256
00:43:57,380 --> 00:43:58,700
(Witness +2)

1257
00:43:58,700 --> 00:43:59,900
(Witness +3)

1258
00:44:01,980 --> 00:44:03,780
(A crowd gathers)

1259
00:44:06,460 --> 00:44:09,300
(Hiding)

1260
00:44:09,380 --> 00:44:10,660
(Watching how things unfold)

1261
00:44:14,420 --> 00:44:17,420
(I peeled mine. Just so you know)

1262
00:44:18,320 --> 00:44:19,200
Those two are suspicious.

1263
00:44:20,580 --> 00:44:22,020
(Getting away from the trouble)

1264
00:44:22,920 --> 00:44:24,520
Fan Chengcheng and Teng...

1265
00:44:26,600 --> 00:44:27,960
Everyone knows
the one-egg-per-room rule,

1266
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:28,960
right?

1267
00:44:28,960 --> 00:44:29,680
Yeah.

1268
00:44:30,720 --> 00:44:31,840
When I walked in,

1269
00:44:31,840 --> 00:44:33,600
Chengcheng rushed to the couch

1270
00:44:33,600 --> 00:44:34,360
and started peeling an egg.

1271
00:44:34,360 --> 00:44:35,680
You shouldn't have come in, Jingyu.

1272
00:44:35,680 --> 00:44:37,320
I saw the whole thing.

1273
00:44:37,320 --> 00:44:37,960
Right?

1274
00:44:37,960 --> 00:44:39,320
I was watching from over there.

1275
00:44:39,320 --> 00:44:41,160
We've got no blind spots between us.

1276
00:44:45,520 --> 00:44:46,600
Teng is back.

1277
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:47,560
It's fine.

1278
00:44:47,560 --> 00:44:48,360
We've got nothing

1279
00:44:48,360 --> 00:44:49,680
to fear.

1280
00:44:52,320 --> 00:44:53,080
I'm going back to peel an egg.

1281
00:44:53,080 --> 00:44:53,950
I'm off to peel an egg.

1282
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:55,120
Off to peel an egg.

1283
00:44:55,340 --> 00:44:57,900
(Killer Zero slips away)

1284
00:45:04,220 --> 00:45:05,860
(Killer One flees the scene)

1285
00:45:06,540 --> 00:45:08,340
(Still clueless, still circling)

1286
00:45:16,300 --> 00:45:17,780
(Bai Jingting's POV)

1287
00:45:31,100 --> 00:45:33,220
(Watching from above)

1288
00:45:33,860 --> 00:45:35,900
(Eyes locked on target)

1289
00:45:38,380 --> 00:45:40,620
(Killer One hunts for a target)

1290
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:42,840
Let's go peel an egg.

1291
00:45:47,360 --> 00:45:47,920
What?

1292
00:45:53,280 --> 00:45:53,800
You're out.

1293
00:45:54,420 --> 00:45:56,380
(Jia Bing is out)

1294
00:45:56,440 --> 00:45:57,200
You're out.

1295
00:45:57,480 --> 00:45:57,920
Go hide.

1296
00:45:59,000 --> 00:45:59,880
Don't hide me in the fridge.

1297
00:46:00,760 --> 00:46:01,040
It's cold.

1298
00:46:01,040 --> 00:46:03,160
This room.

1299
00:46:03,160 --> 00:46:03,760
Hide in this room.

1300
00:46:04,320 --> 00:46:05,320
This room.

1301
00:46:06,660 --> 00:46:07,620
(Saw the whole thing)

1302
00:46:07,620 --> 00:46:08,660
(Ah!)

1303
00:46:09,920 --> 00:46:10,400
Huang Jingyu.

1304
00:46:11,820 --> 00:46:13,060
(Jia Bing, Shen Teng)

1305
00:46:17,320 --> 00:46:18,000
Sit here.

1306
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:19,280
What?

1307
00:46:20,100 --> 00:46:22,400
(Desperately playing it cool)

1308
00:46:22,400 --> 00:46:23,120
Sit here.

1309
00:46:23,860 --> 00:46:25,140
(Shen Teng's POV)

1310
00:46:25,160 --> 00:46:25,880
Sit here.

1311
00:46:27,100 --> 00:46:29,020
(Watching like a hawk)

1312
00:46:29,100 --> 00:46:30,420
(Ah!)

1313
00:46:30,640 --> 00:46:31,480
Sit here.

1314
00:46:31,480 --> 00:46:32,700
(Acting calm)
Keep me company.

1315
00:46:32,720 --> 00:46:33,880
I'm already dead.

1316
00:46:33,880 --> 00:46:35,320
You can't keep me hostage.

1317
00:46:36,820 --> 00:46:39,320
(Defeated)

1318
00:46:39,360 --> 00:46:42,280
(Forced laughter)
That's so dirty, man.

1319
00:46:42,280 --> 00:46:43,600
He's using me

1320
00:46:43,600 --> 00:46:44,900
(Laughing in amusement)
as a hostage

1321
00:46:44,960 --> 00:46:46,120
to throw everyone off.

1322
00:46:46,140 --> 00:46:48,500
(Laughing at his own bad luck)

1323
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:51,000
He even made me sit here.

1324
00:46:51,000 --> 00:46:52,340
(Bitter laugh)

1325
00:46:54,440 --> 00:46:54,800
Huang.

1326
00:46:57,000 --> 00:46:58,720
Bing and Teng are in that room.

1327
00:46:59,280 --> 00:47:00,040
Is one of them dead?

1328
00:47:04,040 --> 00:47:04,920
I think Bing's gone.

1329
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:06,800
Is Bing out?

1330
00:47:07,440 --> 00:47:08,480
Which one of you got eliminated?

1331
00:47:09,100 --> 00:47:10,600
(Both go silent)

1332
00:47:10,600 --> 00:47:12,040
Teng must be a wolf.

1333
00:47:12,520 --> 00:47:13,920
He's probably Killer One.

1334
00:47:14,400 --> 00:47:15,480
We need to catch Killer Zero.

1335
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:16,440
Catch Killer Zero? He's right here.

1336
00:47:18,280 --> 00:47:18,920
Someone's dead.

1337
00:47:18,920 --> 00:47:19,640
(Huang Jingyu's POV)
Let's sound the alarm.

1338
00:47:19,640 --> 00:47:20,400
Who?

1339
00:47:20,400 --> 00:47:21,800
We don't know which one of them is dead.

1340
00:47:22,280 --> 00:47:23,320
Once we sound the alarm,

1341
00:47:23,320 --> 00:47:24,360
we'll find out who it was.

1342
00:47:24,960 --> 00:47:25,800
I'll go do it.

1343
00:47:25,800 --> 00:47:26,800
Go ahead.

1344
00:47:32,660 --> 00:47:35,380
(They sounded the alarm?
I didn't even see anything)

1345
00:47:40,100 --> 00:47:41,900
(All that for nothing)

1346
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:42,520
Who was it?

1347
00:47:43,160 --> 00:47:43,440
No idea.

1348
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:44,160
Someone's dead.

1349
00:47:44,160 --> 00:47:44,920
They told me to sound the alarm.

1350
00:47:45,240 --> 00:47:45,960
Who's out?

1351
00:47:45,960 --> 00:47:47,080
Teng and Bing...

1352
00:47:47,600 --> 00:47:48,120
They're both gone?

1353
00:47:48,840 --> 00:47:49,840
One of them is out.

1354
00:47:50,300 --> 00:47:51,160
(Round 2: First group meeting)

1355
00:47:51,160 --> 00:47:52,920
Let's hear from Song,

1356
00:47:52,920 --> 00:47:54,320
who sounded the alarm.

1357
00:47:54,320 --> 00:47:55,160
Why'd you sound it?

1358
00:47:55,160 --> 00:47:56,400
Hu told me to.

1359
00:47:58,240 --> 00:47:59,040
He told me

1360
00:47:59,040 --> 00:48:00,360
to sound the alarm
because there was a body.

1361
00:48:00,360 --> 00:48:01,480
So you saw it happen?

1362
00:48:01,480 --> 00:48:02,600
When I walked in,

1363
00:48:02,880 --> 00:48:04,440
I saw the whole thing.

1364
00:48:04,680 --> 00:48:07,480
Teng led Bing across the room

1365
00:48:07,480 --> 00:48:08,480
and sat him down.

1366
00:48:08,480 --> 00:48:09,520
Then he said

1367
00:48:09,960 --> 00:48:10,880
something to Bing.

1368
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:13,640
So we had two different angles.

1369
00:48:13,640 --> 00:48:15,280
I was watching them from up high.

1370
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:16,760
(Both saw it from different angles)
You saw Teng

1371
00:48:16,760 --> 00:48:17,800
lead him inside too, right?

1372
00:48:18,200 --> 00:48:18,920
You only saw

1373
00:48:18,920 --> 00:48:21,280
Teng get him to the couch.

1374
00:48:21,280 --> 00:48:22,920
I saw how he got there.

1375
00:48:24,520 --> 00:48:25,960
Then that settles it.

1376
00:48:25,960 --> 00:48:26,640
After that,

1377
00:48:26,640 --> 00:48:28,360
I went over and kept asking.

1378
00:48:28,360 --> 00:48:30,840
But Teng pulled a genius move.

1379
00:48:30,840 --> 00:48:32,080
He played dead.

1380
00:48:35,200 --> 00:48:38,280
I asked if either of them
was still alive.

1381
00:48:39,240 --> 00:48:40,040
Neither said a word.

1382
00:48:40,360 --> 00:48:41,720
Teng spent years trying to make it
in Beijing.

1383
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:43,160
Playing dead is his specialty

1384
00:48:43,160 --> 00:48:43,720
since day one.

1385
00:48:43,780 --> 00:48:44,840
(All those extra roles paid off)

1386
00:48:44,840 --> 00:48:46,480
He started out playing corpses.

1387
00:48:50,320 --> 00:48:51,120
You done acting?

1388
00:48:51,120 --> 00:48:51,880
Are you two done?

1389
00:48:53,440 --> 00:48:54,320
What's your big performance?

1390
00:48:54,580 --> 00:48:56,740
(The stage is yours)

1391
00:48:56,920 --> 00:48:57,840
Churan's out this round.

1392
00:48:58,660 --> 00:48:59,880
(What did I ever do?)

1393
00:48:59,880 --> 00:49:00,600
Churan's out.

1394
00:49:00,740 --> 00:49:03,180
(I'm innocent!)

1395
00:49:03,200 --> 00:49:04,320
Then Churan must be Killer Zero.

1396
00:49:04,320 --> 00:49:05,930
(Churan is acting pretty suspicious)
Churan could be Killer Zero.

1397
00:49:06,520 --> 00:49:07,200
Maybe.

1398
00:49:07,200 --> 00:49:08,360
But we can't.

1399
00:49:08,360 --> 00:49:09,760
Churan was the first one out last round.

1400
00:49:10,160 --> 00:49:10,760
This time...

1401
00:49:11,900 --> 00:49:14,510
Let's protect Churan.

1402
00:49:14,520 --> 00:49:15,400
No first-kill on Churan.

1403
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:17,280
Churan can't go out first again.

1404
00:49:17,600 --> 00:49:19,200
But Teng really is...

1405
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:19,920
way too suspicious.

1406
00:49:20,980 --> 00:49:21,940
(Haha)

1407
00:49:22,540 --> 00:49:23,720
(Haha)

1408
00:49:23,720 --> 00:49:24,960
Why would I be Killer One?

1409
00:49:26,200 --> 00:49:28,320
I told Bing we should take a break.

1410
00:49:28,320 --> 00:49:30,000
Then you came up behind me

1411
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:31,080
and shot him.

1412
00:49:31,140 --> 00:49:33,180
(That's one wild accusation)

1413
00:49:33,200 --> 00:49:35,560
Then you came in and framed me

1414
00:49:35,560 --> 00:49:37,400
as Killer One.

1415
00:49:38,880 --> 00:49:39,520
Teng's right.

1416
00:49:39,520 --> 00:49:40,720
(Convinced in 0.1 seconds)
If he were the bad guy,

1417
00:49:40,720 --> 00:49:41,720
why would he put Bing

1418
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:42,560
on that couch?

1419
00:49:42,560 --> 00:49:43,440
Exactly.

1420
00:49:43,440 --> 00:49:45,400
Why would I put him there?

1421
00:49:45,740 --> 00:49:47,340
(Defending the killer? Bold move)
You're muted for five minutes.

1422
00:49:47,380 --> 00:49:48,900
(What did I do this time?)

1423
00:49:49,760 --> 00:49:51,480
No, here's the thing.

1424
00:49:51,480 --> 00:49:52,680
Was I not clear enough?

1425
00:49:52,680 --> 00:49:53,760
I saw you

1426
00:49:53,760 --> 00:49:54,400
kill him.

1427
00:49:55,720 --> 00:49:56,640
What?

1428
00:49:57,420 --> 00:50:00,060
(Haha)

1429
00:50:00,540 --> 00:50:01,400
(How to act falsely accused)

1430
00:50:01,400 --> 00:50:02,640
Say that again!

1431
00:50:02,640 --> 00:50:03,600
(Fine, I will)
I saw you kill him.

1432
00:50:03,600 --> 00:50:04,560
You helped him over there.

1433
00:50:05,080 --> 00:50:06,400
How did I kill him?

1434
00:50:06,760 --> 00:50:08,200
Come here, Huang Jingyu.

1435
00:50:09,980 --> 00:50:11,600
(Front-row seats to the drama)

1436
00:50:11,600 --> 00:50:12,440
Wow, getting all worked up.

1437
00:50:12,440 --> 00:50:13,640
Keep falsely accusing me,

1438
00:50:13,640 --> 00:50:14,960
and good luck landing

1439
00:50:15,640 --> 00:50:17,040
your next acting gig.

1440
00:50:17,520 --> 00:50:19,760
(Turning up the pressure)
Investors will be wary.

1441
00:50:19,760 --> 00:50:21,120
(Not remotely intimidated)
There's a wall here

1442
00:50:21,120 --> 00:50:22,480
with glass on both sides.

1443
00:50:22,480 --> 00:50:23,880
Hu looked through from here,

1444
00:50:23,880 --> 00:50:25,360
and I looked from over there.

1445
00:50:25,360 --> 00:50:26,120
He saw

1446
00:50:26,120 --> 00:50:27,560
you helping Bing across.

1447
00:50:27,560 --> 00:50:28,280
What I saw

1448
00:50:28,280 --> 00:50:29,360
was why you had to help him.

1449
00:50:29,920 --> 00:50:31,160
I was here, and he was there.

1450
00:50:31,180 --> 00:50:33,200
(How did I miss all of this?)

1451
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:33,840
Who did I help?

1452
00:50:33,840 --> 00:50:34,440
I helped him?

1453
00:50:34,440 --> 00:50:35,600
I was impressed by him last time.

1454
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:36,840
In games like this,

1455
00:50:36,840 --> 00:50:37,480
he's my idol.

1456
00:50:37,480 --> 00:50:38,720
He's my gaming idol.

1457
00:50:41,200 --> 00:50:43,360
Teng is definitely Killer One
this round.

1458
00:50:43,360 --> 00:50:44,480
Let's vote him out first,

1459
00:50:44,480 --> 00:50:45,880
then find Killer Zero.

1460
00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:47,680
Don't vote him out.

1461
00:50:47,680 --> 00:50:49,200
Let's just vote out Killer Zero.

1462
00:50:49,680 --> 00:50:50,880
Who's Killer Zero?

1463
00:50:50,880 --> 00:50:52,000
Before all this,

1464
00:50:52,320 --> 00:50:53,800
I snuck into another room.

1465
00:50:54,680 --> 00:50:56,520
Teng and Chengcheng

1466
00:50:56,520 --> 00:50:58,200
were acting all shady in there.

1467
00:50:58,880 --> 00:51:01,120
Then, when someone came in...

1468
00:51:01,120 --> 00:51:02,640
Even though there was already

1469
00:51:02,640 --> 00:51:04,040
a perfectly peeled egg on the plate,

1470
00:51:04,040 --> 00:51:05,160
Chengcheng suddenly

1471
00:51:05,160 --> 00:51:06,360
sat down on the couch

1472
00:51:06,360 --> 00:51:07,480
and started peeling an egg.

1473
00:51:07,480 --> 00:51:08,520
He peeled a second one.

1474
00:51:08,800 --> 00:51:10,320
You buy that, Hu? Seriously?

1475
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:12,880
Back then,

1476
00:51:12,880 --> 00:51:14,440
Song saw it too.

1477
00:51:14,440 --> 00:51:15,840
We had two different angles.

1478
00:51:15,840 --> 00:51:17,360
I saw this side,
and he saw the other side.

1479
00:51:17,360 --> 00:51:17,920
Man, you...

1480
00:51:18,240 --> 00:51:19,840
You sure saw a lot.

1481
00:51:19,840 --> 00:51:21,200
Two camera angles at every crime scene.

1482
00:51:21,200 --> 00:51:22,140
(Jealous)
Yeah.

1483
00:51:22,160 --> 00:51:23,560
I saw the whole thing.

1484
00:51:25,360 --> 00:51:26,040
Jingyu,

1485
00:51:26,040 --> 00:51:27,560
what if we vote wrong

1486
00:51:27,560 --> 00:51:28,520
and it isn't Chengcheng?

1487
00:51:28,520 --> 00:51:29,200
Then Killer One

1488
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:30,400
is still in the game.

1489
00:51:31,360 --> 00:51:33,160
You only know who Killer One is.

1490
00:51:33,160 --> 00:51:34,560
And I know who Zero is...

1491
00:51:34,560 --> 00:51:35,720
Chengcheng is Killer Zero.

1492
00:51:36,800 --> 00:51:38,120
"Zero" isn't "Killer Cheng".

1493
00:51:40,480 --> 00:51:41,800
No, look. Right now,

1494
00:51:41,800 --> 00:51:43,080
he's definitely Killer One.

1495
00:51:43,560 --> 00:51:44,920
(Killer One)
So it doesn't matter

1496
00:51:44,920 --> 00:51:46,080
if we vote him out this round.

1497
00:51:46,080 --> 00:51:46,880
(Keep him for now)
It does matter.

1498
00:51:46,880 --> 00:51:48,940
(Vote out Killer Zero)
We just need Killer Zero out, right?

1499
00:51:49,200 --> 00:51:50,640
Only Killer One can kill people.

1500
00:51:50,640 --> 00:51:51,960
If we get this vote wrong,

1501
00:51:51,960 --> 00:51:53,200
there won't be another round.

1502
00:51:53,200 --> 00:51:55,240
If we get Killer Zero,
we won't need one.

1503
00:51:55,240 --> 00:51:56,280
If we vote out Killer Zero,

1504
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:56,960
that's game over, right?

1505
00:51:56,960 --> 00:51:57,560
Yeah, game over.

1506
00:51:58,120 --> 00:51:58,840
Yes, it is.

1507
00:51:58,840 --> 00:52:00,080
But what if you're wrong?

1508
00:52:00,480 --> 00:52:01,520
Then we try the next round.

1509
00:52:01,540 --> 00:52:03,020
(Decisive)

1510
00:52:03,060 --> 00:52:04,640
(Cautious)

1511
00:52:04,640 --> 00:52:05,280
Exactly.

1512
00:52:05,640 --> 00:52:06,360
Vote Chengcheng.

1513
00:52:06,800 --> 00:52:08,240
(Feigning betrayal to throw them off)
Think about it.

1514
00:52:08,240 --> 00:52:09,240
If you don't vote for Chengcheng

1515
00:52:09,240 --> 00:52:10,560
and vote me out instead,

1516
00:52:10,560 --> 00:52:12,080
he could infect someone else next round.

1517
00:52:12,080 --> 00:52:13,520
How would you ever solve that?

1518
00:52:15,240 --> 00:52:16,880
He was pretending to be on your side.

1519
00:52:16,880 --> 00:52:17,880
You two were practically blood brothers.

1520
00:52:17,880 --> 00:52:19,400
So you're admitting you're a killer?

1521
00:52:19,400 --> 00:52:20,440
I'm not!

1522
00:52:21,520 --> 00:52:22,480
If you vote me out,

1523
00:52:22,480 --> 00:52:23,320
he could infect someone else?

1524
00:52:23,320 --> 00:52:24,320
How does that make sense?

1525
00:52:24,320 --> 00:52:25,760
It's just an example.

1526
00:52:25,760 --> 00:52:27,240
That's why you can't vote for me.

1527
00:52:27,240 --> 00:52:28,880
You're the wolf.

1528
00:52:31,360 --> 00:52:31,960
Those three...

1529
00:52:31,960 --> 00:52:32,920
Of those three...

1530
00:52:32,920 --> 00:52:33,800
Of those three,

1531
00:52:33,800 --> 00:52:34,800
two have to be involved.

1532
00:52:34,800 --> 00:52:35,520
(Accusing everyone now)
What?

1533
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:36,800
Definitely two of you three.

1534
00:52:37,080 --> 00:52:37,800
What's wrong with us three?

1535
00:52:37,800 --> 00:52:38,920
Am I one of those three?

1536
00:52:40,760 --> 00:52:41,280
Am I...

1537
00:52:41,560 --> 00:52:43,040
Am I one of those three?

1538
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:46,160
Let's just vote out Killer Zero.

1539
00:52:46,840 --> 00:52:47,440
Why wouldn't we get rid

1540
00:52:47,440 --> 00:52:49,480
of the known killer first

1541
00:52:49,480 --> 00:52:51,240
instead of letting them regroup?

1542
00:52:51,240 --> 00:52:52,600
Because our objective

1543
00:52:52,600 --> 00:52:53,600
is to take out Killer Zero.

1544
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:55,760
The game's called Kill Zero.

1545
00:52:55,760 --> 00:52:58,040
We're not even sure who Killer Zero is.

1546
00:52:58,040 --> 00:53:00,240
We should vote out the one we know.

1547
00:53:00,720 --> 00:53:02,080
No, they have to complete a mission.

1548
00:53:02,080 --> 00:53:03,880
If we keep watching him, he can't act.

1549
00:53:03,880 --> 00:53:04,640
Then he...

1550
00:53:04,640 --> 00:53:05,640
They won't be able to strike.

1551
00:53:06,400 --> 00:53:07,200
Bai Jingting is Killer Zero.

1552
00:53:08,600 --> 00:53:09,600
Think about it.

1553
00:53:09,600 --> 00:53:11,040
After Teng got called a wolf,

1554
00:53:11,040 --> 00:53:12,120
he talked to everyone.

1555
00:53:12,120 --> 00:53:13,480
The one person he didn't talk to

1556
00:53:13,480 --> 00:53:14,120
was Bai Jingting.

1557
00:53:16,480 --> 00:53:17,880
So if this round...

1558
00:53:17,880 --> 00:53:19,440
If we're wrong about Chengcheng,

1559
00:53:19,440 --> 00:53:20,920
we can just sound the alarm
and vote him out.

1560
00:53:22,560 --> 00:53:23,320
I barely got to play.

1561
00:53:23,320 --> 00:53:24,560
I didn't even get to do anything,

1562
00:53:24,560 --> 00:53:25,760
and now you're voting me out?

1563
00:53:25,760 --> 00:53:27,860
(Is this how turning 33 starts?)

1564
00:53:27,960 --> 00:53:28,800
Getting a little chilly, huh?

1565
00:53:29,020 --> 00:53:29,800
(Sudden concern)

1566
00:53:29,800 --> 00:53:30,960
Go home and put on a winter coat.

1567
00:53:31,720 --> 00:53:33,080
That's all lace.

1568
00:53:34,600 --> 00:53:35,360
Let's vote Chengcheng out.

1569
00:53:35,360 --> 00:53:37,040
Yeah, vote Chengcheng.

1570
00:53:37,040 --> 00:53:37,880
(Still playing mind games)
Why Chengcheng?

1571
00:53:37,880 --> 00:53:39,360
If Chengcheng really is your boss,

1572
00:53:39,360 --> 00:53:41,240
why would you vote for him?

1573
00:53:41,800 --> 00:53:42,920
That's just how he is!

1574
00:53:43,180 --> 00:53:45,380
(Everyone knows he's trouble)

1575
00:53:45,720 --> 00:53:47,000
Why would he ever agree

1576
00:53:47,000 --> 00:53:48,880
to vote out his own boss?

1577
00:53:49,080 --> 00:53:51,320
Come on, back me up.

1578
00:53:51,320 --> 00:53:52,520
Didn't we both see those two in the room

1579
00:53:52,520 --> 00:53:53,600
from different angles?

1580
00:53:53,600 --> 00:53:54,960
I didn't see it.

1581
00:53:55,400 --> 00:53:56,280
Now you didn't see it?

1582
00:53:56,280 --> 00:53:57,120
Then who did?

1583
00:53:57,120 --> 00:53:57,840
I asked you in the room,

1584
00:53:57,840 --> 00:53:58,880
and you said you saw it!

1585
00:53:58,880 --> 00:54:00,400
I only saw Bing.

1586
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:01,540
I saw it!

1587
00:54:01,540 --> 00:54:02,600
(Completely obsessed)
I saw it!

1588
00:54:02,600 --> 00:54:03,240
Saw what?

1589
00:54:03,240 --> 00:54:05,120
I mean, you saw him with Chengcheng.

1590
00:54:05,120 --> 00:54:06,480
That part I saw.

1591
00:54:06,540 --> 00:54:09,500
(So many witnesses.
Why am I not one of them?)

1592
00:54:09,520 --> 00:54:11,280
Chengcheng was nervously peeling eggs.
Why?

1593
00:54:11,280 --> 00:54:12,320
What's he trying to achieve? Tell me.

1594
00:54:12,320 --> 00:54:13,880
That's suspicious, right?
What's his goal?

1595
00:54:13,880 --> 00:54:15,640
Exactly. I told you he's a bad guy!

1596
00:54:15,640 --> 00:54:16,400
He's an obvious wolf.

1597
00:54:16,400 --> 00:54:17,400
What's he afraid of?

1598
00:54:17,400 --> 00:54:19,000
He's playing it smart.

1599
00:54:20,280 --> 00:54:21,040
Time for a photoshoot. Come on.

1600
00:54:21,580 --> 00:54:24,620
(First day at 33. Life is peaceful)

1601
00:54:24,640 --> 00:54:26,800
Could someone he accuses
really be a bad guy?

1602
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:27,520
Why not?

1603
00:54:27,520 --> 00:54:28,720
That's just how he is.

1604
00:54:29,600 --> 00:54:31,240
Northernmost Beijing, beautiful Huairou.

1605
00:54:31,840 --> 00:54:33,400
(Photoshoot outside)
Wasn't he pretending to be a corpse?

1606
00:54:33,400 --> 00:54:34,200
(Heated argument inside)
Why would he pretend to be a corpse?

1607
00:54:34,200 --> 00:54:35,040
What? We walked in together.

1608
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:36,120
After we sat on the sofa...

1609
00:54:36,120 --> 00:54:36,840
Why would he pretend then?

1610
00:54:36,840 --> 00:54:38,360
He only became a corpse afterward.

1611
00:54:38,360 --> 00:54:39,440
Then you must've done it.

1612
00:54:39,440 --> 00:54:40,840
It wasn't me. He did it.

1613
00:54:40,840 --> 00:54:41,400
Where did he do it?

1614
00:54:41,400 --> 00:54:42,400
He came in behind me.

1615
00:54:42,400 --> 00:54:44,000
He was right in front of me. I saw him.

1616
00:54:44,000 --> 00:54:45,640
How could you? You were outside.

1617
00:54:45,640 --> 00:54:46,760
I saw him right in front of me.

1618
00:54:46,760 --> 00:54:47,480
Oh, give it a rest.

1619
00:54:47,880 --> 00:54:48,760
I was watching him.

1620
00:54:48,920 --> 00:54:50,680
Don't they sound like
old ladies arguing?

1621
00:54:50,680 --> 00:54:51,560
You were outside.

1622
00:54:51,560 --> 00:54:52,400
He was right in front of me.

1623
00:54:52,540 --> 00:54:53,140
(Back off)

1624
00:54:53,500 --> 00:54:54,100
(Ha)

1625
00:54:54,100 --> 00:54:54,700
(Ah)

1626
00:54:54,740 --> 00:54:55,380
(What are you doing?)

1627
00:54:56,140 --> 00:54:56,780
(Back off)

1628
00:54:57,100 --> 00:54:57,740
(Ha)

1629
00:54:57,920 --> 00:54:59,120
I was up against the wall behind you.

1630
00:54:59,120 --> 00:54:59,960
I was watching you the whole time.

1631
00:54:59,960 --> 00:55:00,600
Yeah, you only...

1632
00:55:00,600 --> 00:55:02,460
(Hahaha)

1633
00:55:02,480 --> 00:55:03,600
It's Bai's birthday today.

1634
00:55:05,160 --> 00:55:06,960
Let's all wish him a happy birthday.

1635
00:55:07,400 --> 00:55:09,640
Happy birthday, Bai.

1636
00:55:11,800 --> 00:55:12,760
So, are we voting him out?

1637
00:55:14,200 --> 00:55:15,880
So now,

1638
00:55:15,880 --> 00:55:17,040
we've calmed down a bit, right?

1639
00:55:19,880 --> 00:55:21,280
I think we should

1640
00:55:21,280 --> 00:55:22,640
keep Teng for now.

1641
00:55:22,640 --> 00:55:23,280
Listen.

1642
00:55:23,280 --> 00:55:25,120
Listen to this ridiculous suggestion.

1643
00:55:25,520 --> 00:55:26,840
We should keep Teng?

1644
00:55:26,840 --> 00:55:28,240
Don't insult people.

1645
00:55:28,240 --> 00:55:29,760
That's an insult to my character.

1646
00:55:29,760 --> 00:55:31,640
(Filmed by Hu Xianxu)
When you play games like this,

1647
00:55:31,680 --> 00:55:31,960
you know,

1648
00:55:31,960 --> 00:55:33,800
the worse someone argues their case,

1649
00:55:33,800 --> 00:55:35,240
the more innocent they seem.

1650
00:55:36,740 --> 00:55:37,720
(Something doesn't feel right)

1651
00:55:37,720 --> 00:55:39,000
That's...

1652
00:55:39,680 --> 00:55:41,760
I think your insult is even worse.

1653
00:55:44,520 --> 00:55:45,240
Let's vote Jingyu out.

1654
00:55:45,880 --> 00:55:47,000
You're voting out the "security camera"?

1655
00:55:47,000 --> 00:55:49,160
I've been watching everything,
and you want to vote me out?

1656
00:55:49,160 --> 00:55:50,360
He's filming two shows at once.

1657
00:55:50,360 --> 00:55:51,480
And you're voting him out?

1658
00:55:51,920 --> 00:55:52,320
Exactly.

1659
00:55:52,320 --> 00:55:52,920
He's right here,

1660
00:55:53,640 --> 00:55:54,600
livestreaming.

1661
00:55:54,600 --> 00:55:55,920
Alright, let's decide now.

1662
00:55:55,920 --> 00:55:57,840
Are we voting for Teng, Chengcheng,

1663
00:55:57,840 --> 00:55:58,800
or Bai?

1664
00:55:58,820 --> 00:56:00,920
(Why am I involved?)

1665
00:56:00,920 --> 00:56:01,960
Why would I vote for Chengcheng?

1666
00:56:01,960 --> 00:56:02,800
Did you understand what I said?

1667
00:56:02,800 --> 00:56:03,200
I did.

1668
00:56:03,200 --> 00:56:04,600
I've understood everything.

1669
00:56:04,600 --> 00:56:06,360
I just don't think that's smart.

1670
00:56:06,920 --> 00:56:09,040
Oh, you're so smart.

1671
00:56:09,040 --> 00:56:09,920
You'd vote for an obvious wolf.

1672
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:10,880
Take off your glasses.

1673
00:56:12,720 --> 00:56:13,640
What's there to analyze now?

1674
00:56:14,040 --> 00:56:15,040
Isn't it obviously him?

1675
00:56:15,040 --> 00:56:15,680
I don't know why,

1676
00:56:15,680 --> 00:56:16,920
but I'm feeling the pressure too.

1677
00:56:18,140 --> 00:56:20,700
(Me too)

1678
00:56:21,440 --> 00:56:22,880
I really want to see what happens

1679
00:56:22,880 --> 00:56:23,640
to you guys next round.

1680
00:56:23,880 --> 00:56:24,440
Vote Chengcheng.

1681
00:56:25,880 --> 00:56:26,360
Interesting.

1682
00:56:26,800 --> 00:56:27,600
Let me have another go.

1683
00:56:29,000 --> 00:56:30,600
Let's see if I can get past
those six eyes of yours...

1684
00:56:31,320 --> 00:56:32,400
Wait, is it still me the next round?

1685
00:56:35,000 --> 00:56:35,560
Is that right?

1686
00:56:35,560 --> 00:56:36,280
You've exposed yourself.

1687
00:56:36,280 --> 00:56:38,120
Then we definitely can't vote
for Chengcheng.

1688
00:56:38,840 --> 00:56:39,880
He just said,

1689
00:56:39,880 --> 00:56:42,000
"Vote Chengcheng.
Let me have another go."

1690
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:43,280
That means he's certain

1691
00:56:43,280 --> 00:56:44,120
that if Chengcheng gets voted out,

1692
00:56:44,120 --> 00:56:45,480
he'll still be in the game,

1693
00:56:45,480 --> 00:56:47,040
and the round will continue.

1694
00:56:47,640 --> 00:56:48,520
Isn't he deliberately trying

1695
00:56:48,520 --> 00:56:49,440
to make you read between the lines

1696
00:56:49,440 --> 00:56:50,440
so you won't vote for Chengcheng?

1697
00:56:50,440 --> 00:56:51,960
(Hahaha)
What hidden meaning?

1698
00:56:51,960 --> 00:56:53,560
I said it outright.

1699
00:56:53,560 --> 00:56:54,260
(Hahaha)

1700
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:57,040
Since when was that a hidden message?

1701
00:56:57,040 --> 00:56:58,640
Can I put my glasses back on now?

1702
00:57:00,880 --> 00:57:02,120
I've spotted your weakness.

1703
00:57:06,800 --> 00:57:07,120
Seriously.

1704
00:57:07,120 --> 00:57:07,920
Talking to you guys

1705
00:57:07,920 --> 00:57:09,080
is honestly exhausting.

1706
00:57:14,440 --> 00:57:15,640
I'm just saying, vote for him.

1707
00:57:15,640 --> 00:57:16,520
Give me one more round.

1708
00:57:16,520 --> 00:57:17,680
Just one more round.

1709
00:57:17,680 --> 00:57:18,440
Keep your eyes on me.

1710
00:57:18,440 --> 00:57:19,640
Let's see if I can kill someone else.

1711
00:57:21,320 --> 00:57:22,520
You've given yourself away.

1712
00:57:23,920 --> 00:57:25,040
How have I given myself away?

1713
00:57:26,920 --> 00:57:27,720
You're Killer One.

1714
00:57:28,160 --> 00:57:28,640
Bro.

1715
00:57:28,640 --> 00:57:29,600
We said he was Killer One

1716
00:57:29,600 --> 00:57:31,040
an hour ago.

1717
00:57:32,160 --> 00:57:34,160
Why are you acting
like you're revealing some dark secret?

1718
00:57:36,640 --> 00:57:37,680
You're getting carried away.

1719
00:57:39,800 --> 00:57:40,800
We really can't find Killer Zero.

1720
00:57:40,800 --> 00:57:41,440
We can't.

1721
00:57:41,440 --> 00:57:42,400
We'll never find them.

1722
00:57:42,400 --> 00:57:43,280
Well, if that's what you think,

1723
00:57:43,720 --> 00:57:44,960
you decide today.

1724
00:57:44,960 --> 00:57:45,720
No, you decide.

1725
00:57:45,720 --> 00:57:46,700
(Suddenly being polite)

1726
00:57:47,260 --> 00:57:49,300
(Sudden self-doubt)

1727
00:57:54,760 --> 00:57:56,920
How are you two staying so rational?

1728
00:58:00,440 --> 00:58:02,360
Will you vote for him with me?

1729
00:58:02,360 --> 00:58:03,400
No way.

1730
00:58:03,400 --> 00:58:03,840
Absolutely not.

1731
00:58:03,840 --> 00:58:05,800
No chance.

1732
00:58:07,920 --> 00:58:08,440
Alright.

1733
00:58:09,480 --> 00:58:11,480
Three, two, one. Please vote.

1734
00:58:13,420 --> 00:58:14,540
(Abstain*1, Shen Teng*4,
Wang Churan*1, Huang Jingyu*1)

1735
00:58:14,540 --> 00:58:15,940
(Shen Teng out)

1736
00:58:15,960 --> 00:58:17,160
Teng is eliminated.

1737
00:58:19,300 --> 00:58:20,460
(Shen Teng)

1738
00:58:20,500 --> 00:58:21,440
(You voted for me?)

1739
00:58:21,440 --> 00:58:22,800
The sun's gone down, that's why.

1740
00:58:22,800 --> 00:58:24,800
(Traumatized by voting out wolves)
My mind suddenly cleared up too.

1741
00:58:26,160 --> 00:58:27,200
The mission continues.

1742
00:58:27,840 --> 00:58:29,400
Everyone,
return to your starting points.

1743
00:58:29,940 --> 00:58:31,420
(Song Yaxuan,
Fan Chengcheng, Huang Jingyu)

1744
00:58:31,420 --> 00:58:32,940
(Hu Xianxu, Bai Jingting, Wang Churan)

1745
00:58:33,080 --> 00:58:34,400
Who's Killer Zero?

1746
00:58:34,400 --> 00:58:35,560
Killer Zero...

1747
00:58:36,040 --> 00:58:37,240
I already have

1748
00:58:38,280 --> 00:58:40,040
a prime suspect this round.

1749
00:58:40,880 --> 00:58:41,760
Wang Churan.

1750
00:58:41,780 --> 00:58:42,800
(Suspect: Wang Churan)

1751
00:58:42,800 --> 00:58:44,200
She's been acting sneaky

1752
00:58:44,200 --> 00:58:44,960
and really strange.

1753
00:58:44,960 --> 00:58:46,800
I even saw her heading upstairs alone,

1754
00:58:46,800 --> 00:58:47,920
wandering around for no reason.

1755
00:58:48,480 --> 00:58:50,120
I didn't accuse her earlier

1756
00:58:50,120 --> 00:58:51,960
because I was too busy

1757
00:58:51,960 --> 00:58:53,000
arguing with Jingyu.

1758
00:58:53,060 --> 00:58:57,540
(Got too caught up in the battle
and forgot his original suspect)

1759
00:58:59,020 --> 00:59:00,300
(Killer Zero: Fan Chengcheng)

1760
00:59:00,320 --> 00:59:01,240
What should I do now?

1761
00:59:01,300 --> 00:59:02,860
(Who should I infect next?)

1762
00:59:02,940 --> 00:59:05,780
Mission begins.

1763
00:59:05,880 --> 00:59:06,880
Hu.

1764
00:59:09,200 --> 00:59:10,920
Here's your chance to shine.

1765
00:59:11,800 --> 00:59:12,960
Churan is Killer Zero.

1766
00:59:13,580 --> 00:59:14,860
(Got the big reveal?)
Seriously?

1767
00:59:15,420 --> 00:59:16,580
(Last words from an eliminated player)

1768
00:59:16,600 --> 00:59:17,620
(Don't worry. I'm totally lying)
Don't lie to me.

1769
00:59:19,180 --> 00:59:21,780
(I knew my suspicions were right)

1770
00:59:25,680 --> 00:59:26,800
She's been acting sneaky.

1771
00:59:27,140 --> 00:59:27,840
(That girl's trouble)

1772
00:59:27,840 --> 00:59:28,920
Something's off about her.

1773
00:59:30,100 --> 00:59:31,500
(Better get out of here)

1774
00:59:31,680 --> 00:59:32,760
She's going to kill me.

1775
00:59:35,440 --> 00:59:36,440
Come here. I'll infect you.

1776
00:59:37,740 --> 00:59:40,380
(Same symptoms)

1777
00:59:41,020 --> 00:59:43,100
(I knew Churan was suspicious)

1778
00:59:44,000 --> 00:59:47,360
♪Will we ever meet again?♪

1779
00:59:47,360 --> 00:59:49,340
(I miss you, my Killer One)
♪I prayed before the Buddha♪

1780
00:59:49,340 --> 00:59:51,480
♪For thousands of years♪

1781
00:59:52,200 --> 00:59:55,560
(That's Killer Zero singing)
♪Will we ever meet again?♪

1782
00:59:55,560 --> 00:59:57,420
(Target spotted)
♪I prayed before the Buddha♪

1783
00:59:57,420 --> 00:59:59,680
(Huang Jingyu's POV)
♪For thousands of years♪

1784
01:00:08,820 --> 01:00:11,580
(Huang Jingyu's POV)

1785
01:00:12,140 --> 01:00:14,180
(Forcing him to comply
in the name of justice)

1786
01:00:14,200 --> 01:00:14,960
I'll watch you peel it.

1787
01:00:15,620 --> 01:00:17,020
(Intimidated by Mr. Huang)

1788
01:00:24,120 --> 01:00:24,960
Congratulations.

1789
01:00:25,520 --> 01:00:26,520
You're hired.

1790
01:00:27,840 --> 01:00:28,840
No gesture or anything?

1791
01:00:28,840 --> 01:00:30,580
(Accepts the job in 0.1 seconds)

1792
01:00:31,180 --> 01:00:32,180
(Someone's here. Stay hidden)

1793
01:00:34,000 --> 01:00:34,720
Just wandering around.

1794
01:00:35,480 --> 01:00:36,880
Yeah, Bing is dead.

1795
01:00:37,560 --> 01:00:38,600
There's really no gesture?

1796
01:00:38,600 --> 01:00:39,700
(Asking for a contract)

1797
01:00:43,180 --> 01:00:44,100
(Complete the task with Killer One:
Have them slap the back of your hand while smiling)

1798
01:00:44,100 --> 01:00:44,980
(to unlock the ability to attack)

1799
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:45,240
What?

1800
01:00:45,240 --> 01:00:45,880
How do I kill someone?

1801
01:00:46,760 --> 01:00:48,240
Slap the back of my hand while smiling.

1802
01:00:48,760 --> 01:00:49,560
Hurry up.

1803
01:00:50,440 --> 01:00:51,440
(Killer One: Huang Jingyu)
Then poke someone's dimple

1804
01:00:51,440 --> 01:00:52,760
and say "You're out"
and they'll be dead.

1805
01:00:52,760 --> 01:00:53,540
(Attack method:
Poke their dimple and say "You're out")

1806
01:00:54,400 --> 01:00:55,480
So anyone I catch is dead?

1807
01:00:55,780 --> 01:00:57,620
(Now that he's employed,
he's talking big)

1808
01:00:57,860 --> 01:00:59,820
(Job hunting)

1809
01:01:12,940 --> 01:01:13,620
(Job hunting like a predator)

1810
01:01:13,640 --> 01:01:14,640
You scared me.

1811
01:01:17,520 --> 01:01:18,240
Are you a Good Guy?

1812
01:01:18,580 --> 01:01:20,120
(Applying for a job)

1813
01:01:20,120 --> 01:01:20,720
What?

1814
01:01:20,720 --> 01:01:21,560
It's not you.

1815
01:01:21,760 --> 01:01:23,000
You really want to get infected, huh?

1816
01:01:23,000 --> 01:01:24,140
(Sorry to disappoint you)

1817
01:01:26,860 --> 01:01:29,180
(Off to find a job)

1818
01:01:34,320 --> 01:01:35,000
Time to peel an egg.

1819
01:01:35,060 --> 01:01:36,380
(Egg-verything will go smoothly)

1820
01:01:40,040 --> 01:01:41,080
The most perfectly peeled egg yet.

1821
01:01:41,700 --> 01:01:42,580
(Good Guy Task Progress: 1/7)

1822
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:43,200
That feels amazing.

1823
01:01:43,340 --> 01:01:44,600
(Egg-peeling skills upgraded)

1824
01:01:44,600 --> 01:01:45,200
You've peeled it?

1825
01:01:46,320 --> 01:01:46,920
You've peeled it?

1826
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:48,480
What?

1827
01:01:49,880 --> 01:01:50,600
Have you peeled it?

1828
01:01:50,600 --> 01:01:51,160
Yeah.

1829
01:01:52,880 --> 01:01:53,280
Good job.

1830
01:01:53,280 --> 01:01:54,220
(Looking around)

1831
01:01:54,260 --> 01:01:54,940
(Huang Jingyu's POV)

1832
01:01:54,940 --> 01:01:55,660
(No witnesses in sight)

1833
01:01:56,640 --> 01:01:57,200
You're out.

1834
01:01:57,200 --> 01:01:58,160
Come on, over here.

1835
01:02:04,000 --> 01:02:04,440
Get inside.

1836
01:02:05,920 --> 01:02:06,240
Crouch down.

1837
01:02:07,200 --> 01:02:07,680
Stay there.

1838
01:02:08,100 --> 01:02:09,940
(Song Yaxuan OUT)

1839
01:02:10,980 --> 01:02:13,060
(Sabotaging the task while he's at it)

1840
01:02:13,380 --> 01:02:15,100
(Making sure nobody noticed)

1841
01:02:15,940 --> 01:02:16,860
(Fleeing the crime scene)

1842
01:02:17,460 --> 01:02:18,860
(Effortlessly keeping a straight face)

1843
01:02:19,960 --> 01:02:21,560
I think I just saw Song go in here.

1844
01:02:22,480 --> 01:02:23,880
He's acting a little strange this round.

1845
01:02:23,900 --> 01:02:27,020
(No longer able to defend himself)

1846
01:02:27,040 --> 01:02:27,960
Is Song in here?

1847
01:02:30,360 --> 01:02:31,080
You're dead.

1848
01:02:31,220 --> 01:02:33,220
(Surprise. It's Song behind the door)

1849
01:02:38,580 --> 01:02:39,500
(Wait a second)

1850
01:02:39,780 --> 01:02:42,460
(There was definitely
someone here earlier)

1851
01:02:43,260 --> 01:02:45,260
(Who killed our Shandong boy?)

1852
01:02:45,300 --> 01:02:47,020
(Wang Churan's POV)

1853
01:02:48,880 --> 01:02:49,640
Who's there?

1854
01:02:51,820 --> 01:02:54,620
(Wang Churan's POV)

1855
01:02:54,640 --> 01:02:55,760
Who's in there?

1856
01:03:00,320 --> 01:03:01,960
Everyone, come to this room. Quick.

1857
01:03:01,960 --> 01:03:02,640
(Requesting backup)

1858
01:03:02,640 --> 01:03:03,280
Hurry.

1859
01:03:03,680 --> 01:03:04,680
Hurry up.

1860
01:03:04,680 --> 01:03:05,300
(Requesting backup)

1861
01:03:08,640 --> 01:03:10,400
I think I've figured it out.

1862
01:03:10,860 --> 01:03:12,860
(Teng probably wasn't lying)
Wang Churan

1863
01:03:12,960 --> 01:03:14,400
is Killer Zero.

1864
01:03:14,620 --> 01:03:15,580
Quick.

1865
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:17,920
Everyone, get to this room!

1866
01:03:18,300 --> 01:03:19,320
(What's she up to now?)

1867
01:03:19,320 --> 01:03:20,080
Hurry.

1868
01:03:21,520 --> 01:03:23,520
Everyone, come to this room!

1869
01:03:24,400 --> 01:03:25,360
Song is dead.

1870
01:03:26,040 --> 01:03:26,480
What?

1871
01:03:26,840 --> 01:03:27,880
Song is dead.

1872
01:03:28,080 --> 01:03:28,520
Where?

1873
01:03:29,040 --> 01:03:30,000
Right here.

1874
01:03:30,020 --> 01:03:31,940
(Even more convinced Churan is suspicious)

1875
01:03:36,600 --> 01:03:37,920
Someone's hiding upstairs.

1876
01:03:37,940 --> 01:03:38,940
(Brushed off without a second thought)
It's probably Chengcheng.

1877
01:03:40,440 --> 01:03:41,320
I don't know.

1878
01:03:41,320 --> 01:03:42,740
(It's still a horror movie over here)
Someone come upstairs with me.

1879
01:03:42,920 --> 01:03:44,510
(Paranoia kicking in)
What if you kill me up there?

1880
01:03:44,520 --> 01:03:45,680
We won't. We'll all be witnesses.

1881
01:03:49,800 --> 01:03:50,440
There's nobody here.

1882
01:03:51,120 --> 01:03:51,680
Nobody.

1883
01:03:52,600 --> 01:03:54,240
Must've been a crew member.

1884
01:03:54,480 --> 01:03:55,440
Scared ourselves for nothing.

1885
01:03:55,540 --> 01:03:57,700
(Another misunderstanding)

1886
01:03:57,720 --> 01:03:59,080
So Song's gone?

1887
01:03:59,080 --> 01:04:00,320
Song's out.

1888
01:04:00,320 --> 01:04:01,320
Let's sound the alarm.

1889
01:04:01,720 --> 01:04:02,560
Sound the alarm.

1890
01:04:02,580 --> 01:04:04,660
(Preparing his defense early)

1891
01:04:05,080 --> 01:04:05,520
Let's go.

1892
01:04:05,900 --> 01:04:07,040
(Second group meeting)
I just saw

1893
01:04:07,040 --> 01:04:07,640
a bunch of people

1894
01:04:07,640 --> 01:04:09,560
(Cutting in first)
busy hiding a body.

1895
01:04:09,720 --> 01:04:11,400
So I thought
someone must've been killed.

1896
01:04:11,720 --> 01:04:12,400
When I entered the room,

1897
01:04:12,400 --> 01:04:14,520
I found Song hidden

1898
01:04:15,120 --> 01:04:16,280
inside a little black storage room.

1899
01:04:16,680 --> 01:04:18,120
I was pretty far away,
so I couldn't see clearly.

1900
01:04:18,120 --> 01:04:19,120
Then I saw a group of people

1901
01:04:19,120 --> 01:04:20,680
running upstairs.

1902
01:04:20,680 --> 01:04:22,040
I was afraid I'd get killed

1903
01:04:22,400 --> 01:04:23,160
if I went up alone.

1904
01:04:23,360 --> 01:04:24,920
So I called everyone over to back me up

1905
01:04:24,920 --> 01:04:26,120
while I checked upstairs.

1906
01:04:26,800 --> 01:04:27,800
But it turned out

1907
01:04:27,800 --> 01:04:28,480
to be the crew.

1908
01:04:28,600 --> 01:04:29,360
(All that buildup for nothing?)

1909
01:04:29,360 --> 01:04:30,480
And there was no killer.

1910
01:04:30,620 --> 01:04:32,380
(What a waste of attention)

1911
01:04:33,560 --> 01:04:35,440
I was completely hooked.

1912
01:04:36,520 --> 01:04:37,240
Wait...

1913
01:04:37,240 --> 01:04:38,480
There's a plot twist.

1914
01:04:38,480 --> 01:04:39,910
(Let's hear the rest)
Right. That's why

1915
01:04:39,920 --> 01:04:40,960
I gathered everyone here.

1916
01:04:41,920 --> 01:04:43,480
But I've noticed

1917
01:04:43,480 --> 01:04:45,040
one major problem.

1918
01:04:51,080 --> 01:04:52,840
At both crime scenes,

1919
01:04:52,840 --> 01:04:54,160
there was someone

1920
01:04:54,160 --> 01:04:55,840
standing unusually close.

1921
01:04:57,320 --> 01:04:58,320
And that person was Hu.

1922
01:04:58,780 --> 01:04:59,620
(Not even surprised anymore)

1923
01:05:00,540 --> 01:05:01,620
(The guilty one strikes first?)

1924
01:05:01,760 --> 01:05:02,760
He was near both

1925
01:05:02,760 --> 01:05:04,280
crime scenes.

1926
01:05:04,280 --> 01:05:04,840
Really close, in fact.

1927
01:05:07,940 --> 01:05:09,220
(Bro, it's her)

1928
01:05:09,260 --> 01:05:10,820
(See? I told you)

1929
01:05:12,480 --> 01:05:13,480
I can't take this anymore.

1930
01:05:13,480 --> 01:05:15,500
(I can't take it. Just kidding.
My big moment is coming)

1931
01:05:18,240 --> 01:05:19,320
I seriously never want

1932
01:05:19,320 --> 01:05:20,760
to play Werewolf again.

1933
01:05:20,760 --> 01:05:22,300
(Waiting for his big moment)

1934
01:05:25,120 --> 01:05:26,260
(My brain's fried)
It's mentally exhausting,

1935
01:05:26,260 --> 01:05:27,520
(Worth it)
and I've lost my voice.

1936
01:05:27,520 --> 01:05:29,260
(My voice is gone. Totally worth it)
And it's emotionally draining.

1937
01:05:29,260 --> 01:05:30,420
(My heart's in pieces. Worth every second)
You know?

1938
01:05:30,940 --> 01:05:33,240
(Laughing through tears)

1939
01:05:33,240 --> 01:05:35,520
Why do I put myself
through this every day?

1940
01:05:36,220 --> 01:05:38,860
(These tears are fake.
Waiting for my big moment)

1941
01:05:44,560 --> 01:05:45,800
Exactly. I just think

1942
01:05:45,800 --> 01:05:46,640
Hu's acting suspicious.

1943
01:05:46,640 --> 01:05:48,180
(Unfazed by anything)

1944
