2269
01:16:10,360 --> 01:16:10,760
Come here.

2270
01:16:10,760 --> 01:16:11,560
(Still looking for something to do)

2271
01:16:11,560 --> 01:16:12,440
Give me something to do.

2272
01:16:12,720 --> 01:16:14,560
Let me find something for you to do.

2273
01:16:14,560 --> 01:16:16,200
Cut the scallions into short lengths.

2274
01:16:16,760 --> 01:16:17,200
All right.

2275
01:16:17,260 --> 01:16:18,900
(Getting to work)

2276
01:16:19,100 --> 01:16:21,260
(Preparing scallion-braised tofu)

2277
01:16:21,400 --> 01:16:22,320
Watch your fingers.

2278
01:16:22,320 --> 01:16:22,680
I am fine.

2279
01:16:22,680 --> 01:16:25,460
(Cut the scallions into sections
and the tofu into cubes. Set aside)

2280
01:16:26,880 --> 01:16:27,640
Today, we're having

2281
01:16:27,980 --> 01:16:29,840
Qiang-style hot pot broth base.

2282
01:16:29,840 --> 01:16:30,400
Qiang-style hot pot.

2283
01:16:30,400 --> 01:16:31,560
Cuan-style hot pot broth base.

2284
01:16:31,560 --> 01:16:32,560
Qiang-style hot pot broth base.

2285
01:16:33,600 --> 01:16:34,560
Bai, what are you making?

2286
01:16:37,520 --> 01:16:39,080
Are you afraid
I will steal Bing's spotlight?

2287
01:16:39,340 --> 01:16:40,580
(A needless concern)

2288
01:16:40,720 --> 01:16:42,320
There is no need to worry about that.

2289
01:16:42,340 --> 01:16:44,040
(He knows better than to say it)

2290
01:16:44,040 --> 01:16:45,240
Did you really have to say that?

2291
01:16:45,240 --> 01:16:46,200
What are you making?

2292
01:16:46,200 --> 01:16:47,720
I want to make scallion-braised tofu.

2293
01:16:48,720 --> 01:16:49,920
Are you ordering takeout, or...?

2294
01:16:52,920 --> 01:16:54,040
Now that we're in Beijing,

2295
01:16:54,040 --> 01:16:56,440
you are ordering takeout
and pretending you cooked it yourself.

2296
01:16:59,360 --> 01:17:00,680
Is there anything I can help you with?

2297
01:17:00,680 --> 01:17:01,360
No.

2298
01:17:01,360 --> 01:17:02,560
Bai, it is your birthday today.

2299
01:17:02,560 --> 01:17:03,160
You don't have to do anything.

2300
01:17:03,160 --> 01:17:04,040
Just relax.

2301
01:17:05,300 --> 01:17:07,620
(Birthday privileges)

2302
01:17:09,800 --> 01:17:11,960
I learned how to make eggs
with scallions yesterday.

2303
01:17:13,200 --> 01:17:14,120
Looks like we picked the same dish.

2304
01:17:14,120 --> 01:17:15,360
We chose almost exactly the same thing.

2305
01:17:15,760 --> 01:17:17,320
It's your birthday,
so you call the shots.

2306
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:19,320
If you want to make eggs with scallions,

2307
01:17:19,320 --> 01:17:21,120
I can use this tofu
to make something else.

2308
01:17:21,140 --> 01:17:21,800
(At least I know how to read the room)

2309
01:17:21,800 --> 01:17:22,340
You make it.

2310
01:17:22,360 --> 01:17:23,000
You

2311
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:23,960
can make it for me.

2312
01:17:24,280 --> 01:17:25,120
That works.

2313
01:17:26,420 --> 01:17:28,260
(The scallions have been cut)

2314
01:17:29,120 --> 01:17:30,160
Did I cut these scallions properly?

2315
01:17:30,560 --> 01:17:31,200
Yes, that is fine.

2316
01:17:31,760 --> 01:17:32,640
What are those black specks on them?

2317
01:17:33,280 --> 01:17:33,720
Scallions.

2318
01:17:35,400 --> 01:17:36,880
You did not wash off the dirt.

2319
01:17:37,400 --> 01:17:38,100
Wash them again.

2320
01:17:38,140 --> 01:17:39,340
(Sent back to redo the work)

2321
01:17:40,420 --> 01:17:42,860
(Washing them again)

2322
01:17:45,340 --> 01:17:47,100
(Inspecting them carefully)

2323
01:17:50,040 --> 01:17:51,360
What mischief are you getting into now?

2324
01:17:52,360 --> 01:17:55,040
(Studying the cooking tutorial intently)
I am checking the recipe.

2325
01:17:55,520 --> 01:17:57,320
I am looking up a cooking tutorial.

2326
01:17:59,380 --> 01:18:00,940
(Coming over to help with the cooking)

2327
01:18:02,700 --> 01:18:04,260
(Bing is completely focused
on preparing the food)

2328
01:18:06,840 --> 01:18:08,200
What are you making, Bing?

2329
01:18:08,440 --> 01:18:09,920
(Dumplings and copper-pot hot pot)
Dumplings and hot pot.

2330
01:18:09,920 --> 01:18:11,400
(Chicken and glass noodle stew)
And chicken and glass noodles stew.

2331
01:18:11,400 --> 01:18:12,120
(Northeastern mixed stew)
And a Northeastern mixed stew.

2332
01:18:13,360 --> 01:18:14,600
What about you? What are you making?

2333
01:18:15,840 --> 01:18:16,760
Cola chicken wings.

2334
01:18:17,440 --> 01:18:18,000
What?

2335
01:18:18,700 --> 01:18:19,740
(Cola chicken wings)

2336
01:18:21,260 --> 01:18:23,900
(We share the same favorite dish)

2337
01:18:23,920 --> 01:18:24,800
Why does that sound

2338
01:18:25,720 --> 01:18:26,840
so familiar?

2339
01:18:27,120 --> 01:18:28,080
Cola chicken wings.

2340
01:18:28,720 --> 01:18:30,840
Are you trying to recreate
that famous chef's recipe?

2341
01:18:30,840 --> 01:18:31,580
(The chicken wings
that went viral in Season 3)

2342
01:18:32,360 --> 01:18:33,360
I am going to do it better than him.

2343
01:18:33,360 --> 01:18:34,860
(A declaration of challenge)

2344
01:18:37,520 --> 01:18:38,760
I am reserving this pot.

2345
01:18:39,480 --> 01:18:41,240
Song, are you cooking?

2346
01:18:42,480 --> 01:18:43,200
I'll help with the prep.

2347
01:18:43,920 --> 01:18:44,840
I'll be your assistant's assistant.

2348
01:18:44,840 --> 01:18:45,820
(Assistant and assistant's assistant)

2349
01:18:46,360 --> 01:18:47,000
I will help you.

2350
01:18:47,000 --> 01:18:47,600
Go wash these.

2351
01:18:48,760 --> 01:18:49,720
You have washed these already, right?

2352
01:18:49,720 --> 01:18:50,840
Yes.

2353
01:18:51,240 --> 01:18:51,880
All right, then.

2354
01:18:52,040 --> 01:18:53,120
Bing, I washed

2355
01:18:53,120 --> 01:18:53,860
(Taking credit for someone else's work)
these for you.

2356
01:18:53,880 --> 01:18:54,360
Good job.

2357
01:18:56,160 --> 01:18:56,840
No, wait.

2358
01:18:56,840 --> 01:18:57,880
These are for this side.

2359
01:18:58,680 --> 01:18:59,360
That side?

2360
01:19:02,080 --> 01:19:03,080
Hu, I have washed these for you.

2361
01:19:04,240 --> 01:19:05,400
Didn't Song wash these?

2362
01:19:05,720 --> 01:19:06,280
Yes.

2363
01:19:06,340 --> 01:19:09,020
(You're welcome)
He already brought these over earlier.

2364
01:19:09,120 --> 01:19:09,840
He washed them again?

2365
01:19:10,040 --> 01:19:10,960
They were not washed properly.

2366
01:19:10,960 --> 01:19:11,840
Not clean enough.

2367
01:19:13,300 --> 01:19:14,820
(Scallion-braised tofu)

2368
01:19:14,820 --> 01:19:16,620
(Pan-fry the tofu
until golden brown on both sides)

2369
01:19:20,540 --> 01:19:23,140
(Is it ready?)

2370
01:19:23,160 --> 01:19:24,560
Why is it falling apart again?

2371
01:19:24,880 --> 01:19:26,040
I flipped it too soon.

2372
01:19:26,040 --> 01:19:26,760
The pieces are all sticking together.

2373
01:19:26,760 --> 01:19:28,200
How am I supposed to flip them?

2374
01:19:28,200 --> 01:19:29,960
The instructions said
to pan-fry the tofu.

2375
01:19:29,960 --> 01:19:31,440
That does not mean
you should deep-fry it.

2376
01:19:32,160 --> 01:19:33,360
Are you making stinky tofu?

2377
01:19:35,840 --> 01:19:36,480
Why don't you

2378
01:19:36,480 --> 01:19:37,780
(You may leave now)
go back to your room and warm up?

2379
01:19:39,240 --> 01:19:40,680
Song is quick with his comebacks.

2380
01:19:41,240 --> 01:19:42,800
He is putting all his effort

2381
01:19:42,800 --> 01:19:45,040
into making fun of us.

2382
01:19:45,100 --> 01:19:46,980
(Teasing)

2383
01:19:47,260 --> 01:19:48,960
(Back to the matter at hand)

2384
01:19:48,960 --> 01:19:51,120
Did I use the wrong kind of tofu,

2385
01:19:51,120 --> 01:19:52,080
or did I do something wrong?

2386
01:19:52,760 --> 01:19:54,120
(Dark and crumbling)
How did it turn out like this?

2387
01:19:54,120 --> 01:19:55,520
You did not even add soy sauce.

2388
01:19:55,520 --> 01:19:57,120
(A merciless remark)
Why is it so dark?

2389
01:19:58,100 --> 01:19:59,540
(Trying not to laugh again)

2390
01:20:01,460 --> 01:20:04,340
(Muting himself to keep
from saying something hurtful)

2391
01:20:05,960 --> 01:20:08,280
Go away.

2392
01:20:08,840 --> 01:20:09,320
All right.

2393
01:20:09,320 --> 01:20:10,060
Get a close-up.

2394
01:20:10,060 --> 01:20:11,340
(Camera assistant reporting for duty)

2395
01:20:11,420 --> 01:20:14,020
(Bai Jingting's point of view)

2396
01:20:14,480 --> 01:20:16,720
Why is it sticking to the pan
so much this time?

2397
01:20:17,320 --> 01:20:17,920
Is this tofu pudding?

2398
01:20:17,920 --> 01:20:18,800
The pan is the problem.

2399
01:20:19,820 --> 01:20:22,100
(An awkward apology)

2400
01:20:22,160 --> 01:20:23,750
(Not an apology at all)
You must have added soy sauce.

2401
01:20:23,760 --> 01:20:24,800
Otherwise, it would not
have turned out this dark.

2402
01:20:24,820 --> 01:20:26,000
(So dark)

2403
01:20:26,000 --> 01:20:27,200
Save the crispy bits for me.

2404
01:20:27,440 --> 01:20:28,160
Pan-fried crispy tofu.

2405
01:20:28,160 --> 01:20:29,560
(Pan-fried crispy tofu)

2406
01:20:29,560 --> 01:20:31,080
I actually like my food a little burnt.

2407
01:20:31,240 --> 01:20:32,080
That is what I like about Song.

2408
01:20:32,720 --> 01:20:33,120
Right?

2409
01:20:33,120 --> 01:20:33,720
Unlike you!

2410
01:20:34,840 --> 01:20:36,160
It is your birthday today.

2411
01:20:36,840 --> 01:20:37,480
What about it?

2412
01:20:38,440 --> 01:20:39,680
I will let you off this time.

2413
01:20:39,680 --> 01:20:40,980
(I will spare you for now)

2414
01:20:42,720 --> 01:20:44,080
(Cola chicken wings are up next)
We will get to the cola chicken wings soon.

2415
01:20:44,100 --> 01:20:45,900
(Looking forward to it)

2416
01:20:51,240 --> 01:20:52,280
I have already reserved that pot.

2417
01:20:52,820 --> 01:20:54,000
(Can you actually reserve a pot?)

2418
01:20:54,000 --> 01:20:55,360
Can I borrow it to blanch something?

2419
01:20:55,800 --> 01:20:57,000
I have already claimed it.

2420
01:20:57,000 --> 01:20:58,520
You can use the steamer
over there to blanch it.

2421
01:21:00,120 --> 01:21:00,640
Over there...

2422
01:21:00,640 --> 01:21:01,360
(No room for me)

2423
01:21:01,360 --> 01:21:02,080
I feel like...

2424
01:21:03,040 --> 01:21:04,980
(Still trying to negotiate)
Can I blanch something in this pot?

2425
01:21:05,400 --> 01:21:05,920
No.

2426
01:21:06,660 --> 01:21:08,160
(Just teasing)

2427
01:21:08,160 --> 01:21:09,040
Be polite.

2428
01:21:09,720 --> 01:21:10,280
Thank you.

2429
01:21:13,360 --> 01:21:14,320
As for cola chicken wings,

2430
01:21:14,320 --> 01:21:15,480
if you are willing

2431
01:21:15,480 --> 01:21:16,280
to learn,

2432
01:21:16,280 --> 01:21:17,640
I could teach you.

2433
01:21:17,640 --> 01:21:19,320
Were you looking it up the whole time?

2434
01:21:19,520 --> 01:21:20,580
(Not at all)
No.

2435
01:21:20,600 --> 01:21:22,440
I already know the recipe by heart.

2436
01:21:22,960 --> 01:21:24,480
What did you call
your chicken wings again?

2437
01:21:24,680 --> 01:21:26,580
(Looking rather embarrassed)
Gummy chicken wings or whatever?

2438
01:21:26,880 --> 01:21:27,600
Gummy?

2439
01:21:27,600 --> 01:21:28,960
No.

2440
01:21:28,980 --> 01:21:30,760
Candied chicken wings.

2441
01:21:30,760 --> 01:21:31,960
Candied...

2442
01:21:33,000 --> 01:21:33,800
Seriously?

2443
01:21:34,020 --> 01:21:34,880
(That really happened)

2444
01:21:34,880 --> 01:21:36,000
They were sticking to my chin.

2445
01:21:36,600 --> 01:21:37,480
What are you talking about?

2446
01:21:40,440 --> 01:21:40,880
Bing.

2447
01:21:41,600 --> 01:21:42,840
Could you take a look?

2448
01:21:43,080 --> 01:21:43,960
Sure. Just a moment.

2449
01:21:44,080 --> 01:21:45,040
Is this ready?

2450
01:21:45,760 --> 01:21:47,040
You did not use enough oil,

2451
01:21:47,040 --> 01:21:47,560
Hu.

2452
01:21:48,240 --> 01:21:48,680
Stir-fry it a little longer.

2453
01:21:48,680 --> 01:21:49,800
Let the edges turn slightly golden.

2454
01:21:49,960 --> 01:21:51,480
Then add the sauce.

2455
01:21:51,680 --> 01:21:54,280
How much of each ingredient
goes into the sauce?

2456
01:21:54,280 --> 01:21:55,920
Just a little. A pinch will do.

2457
01:21:58,720 --> 01:21:59,680
Can you smell the aroma?

2458
01:22:00,320 --> 01:22:01,360
Once you can smell it, add the sauce.

2459
01:22:01,360 --> 01:22:02,200
That should be enough.

2460
01:22:02,440 --> 01:22:04,120
I have always had trouble

2461
01:22:04,120 --> 01:22:05,840
figuring out what Bing means

2462
01:22:05,840 --> 01:22:07,240
when he says a little.

2463
01:22:07,240 --> 01:22:08,960
Every time he says a little,

2464
01:22:09,400 --> 01:22:10,600
it turns out to be...

2465
01:22:11,440 --> 01:22:13,000
(A generous amount of a little)
Add a little soy sauce as well.

2466
01:22:13,160 --> 01:22:14,160
Add some steamed fish soy sauce too.

2467
01:22:14,160 --> 01:22:15,080
And a little five-spice powder.

2468
01:22:17,380 --> 01:22:18,780
(Focused)
The ingredients are fragrant now.

2469
01:22:18,800 --> 01:22:20,160
Once they are fragrant,
add boiling water.

2470
01:22:20,440 --> 01:22:21,160
How much should I add?

2471
01:22:21,160 --> 01:22:21,560
Add...

2472
01:22:23,280 --> 01:22:23,720
All right.

2473
01:22:24,560 --> 01:22:25,000
All right.

2474
01:22:25,240 --> 01:22:26,360
Put the tofu in and let it simmer.

2475
01:22:28,460 --> 01:22:30,300
(Scallion-braised tofu, simmering away)

2476
01:22:30,640 --> 01:22:31,840
Since they're not eating
my cooking anyway,

2477
01:22:31,840 --> 01:22:33,200
why don't I make dinner for two?

2478
01:22:33,200 --> 01:22:34,200
(An invitation to try his cooking)
Let us have a taste first.

2479
01:22:34,400 --> 01:22:35,160
Instant noodles?

2480
01:22:35,560 --> 01:22:36,460
A beef rice bowl.

2481
01:22:36,460 --> 01:22:37,880
(Fan-style beef rice bowl
successfully loaded)

2482
01:22:37,880 --> 01:22:38,280
Seriously?

2483
01:22:42,280 --> 01:22:42,840
All right.

2484
01:22:42,840 --> 01:22:43,760
Here comes the grand entrance.

2485
01:22:43,760 --> 01:22:44,320
That will do.

2486
01:22:44,760 --> 01:22:45,400
Just wait and see.

2487
01:22:45,960 --> 01:22:46,440
All right.

2488
01:22:46,440 --> 01:22:48,480
(Time to show what I can do)

2489
01:22:48,480 --> 01:22:49,400
Let me borrow

2490
01:22:49,400 --> 01:22:49,800
