2491
01:22:49,800 --> 01:22:50,400
That is my pot.

2492
01:22:50,960 --> 01:22:51,560
Weren't you still chopping?

2493
01:22:51,560 --> 01:22:52,400
I just got it back.

2494
01:22:53,040 --> 01:22:53,920
Can I use it to blanch something?

2495
01:22:54,840 --> 01:22:56,360
I got it back after someone
finished blanching earlier.

2496
01:22:57,080 --> 01:22:57,720
Move aside.

2497
01:22:59,360 --> 01:23:00,200
Move aside.

2498
01:23:00,200 --> 01:23:01,120
The flames are shooting up.

2499
01:23:02,840 --> 01:23:03,280
What happened?

2500
01:23:05,540 --> 01:23:09,500
(Putting out the fire)

2501
01:23:12,960 --> 01:23:14,080
Forget the stir-frying.
That's the least of our worries.

2502
01:23:14,080 --> 01:23:15,520
I just saved all your lives.

2503
01:23:15,520 --> 01:23:16,040
I am serious.

2504
01:23:17,800 --> 01:23:20,440
Teng, we have truly been
through life and death together.

2505
01:23:20,440 --> 01:23:21,120
We have been through...

2506
01:23:21,120 --> 01:23:21,840
What on earth is this?

2507
01:23:23,100 --> 01:23:24,860
(An improvised stew is now in the works)

2508
01:23:24,900 --> 01:23:26,260
(Stir-fry scallions and garlic
until fragrant, then remove them)

2509
01:23:26,300 --> 01:23:27,620
(Render the fat from the pork belly,
then add the vegetables one at a time)

2510
01:23:27,660 --> 01:23:28,460
(Add soy sauces,
salt, and dried chili peppers)

2511
01:23:28,580 --> 01:23:30,620
(Stir well, then add
the eggplant and pork ribs)

2512
01:23:30,660 --> 01:23:32,420
(Stir-fry briefly,
then add boiling water)

2513
01:23:33,800 --> 01:23:34,520
Where is my spatula?

2514
01:23:35,780 --> 01:23:38,580
(I managed to keep the pot
but lost my spatula)

2515
01:23:40,980 --> 01:23:43,300
(Making do with whatever is available)

2516
01:23:48,460 --> 01:23:49,620
(Simmer for 40 minutes)

2517
01:23:49,720 --> 01:23:50,720
Let me show everyone what proper

2518
01:23:50,720 --> 01:23:52,820
(Cola chicken wings)
cola chicken wings should taste like.

2519
01:23:54,540 --> 01:23:56,020
(Pan-fry the blanched chicken wings
until golden brown on both sides)

2520
01:23:57,060 --> 01:23:59,540
(Add light and dark soy sauce,
then fry until fragrant)

2521
01:24:00,040 --> 01:24:00,960
Don't you need to turn them over?

2522
01:24:01,760 --> 01:24:02,280
It is fine.

2523
01:24:03,040 --> 01:24:04,580
(I have my own rhythm)
I know exactly what I am doing.

2524
01:24:05,100 --> 01:24:07,700
(Add cola, simmer for 20 minutes,
then reduce over high heat)

2525
01:24:11,620 --> 01:24:12,820
(Freestyle stew, Cola chicken wings)

2526
01:24:12,820 --> 01:24:14,060
(Beef rice bowl,
Chicken and glass noodle stew)

2527
01:24:14,100 --> 01:24:17,300
(Bing prepares
chicken and glass noodle stew)

2528
01:24:17,340 --> 01:24:19,220
(Once lightly seared,
stir-fry the ingredients)

2529
01:24:19,600 --> 01:24:20,540
(Fan-style beef rice bowl,
preparing the sauce)

2530
01:24:20,540 --> 01:24:21,840
I think I will add some beef seasoning.

2531
01:24:21,840 --> 01:24:22,720
After all,

2532
01:24:22,720 --> 01:24:23,520
that is what

2533
01:24:23,520 --> 01:24:24,840
my online cooking instructors recommend.

2534
01:24:24,940 --> 01:24:26,640
(My online cooking instructors)

2535
01:24:26,640 --> 01:24:28,120
You can leave it out
if you do not like it.

2536
01:24:29,620 --> 01:24:31,080
(Add the beef and onions
to the pan one at a time)

2537
01:24:31,080 --> 01:24:32,960
It is time to try something different.

2538
01:24:34,680 --> 01:24:36,960
Quick, get me a spatula.

2539
01:24:37,640 --> 01:24:40,220
(Urgently searching for a spatula)
Quick, get me a spatula.

2540
01:24:43,300 --> 01:24:44,320
(Ran gets all the praise)
Hurry up.

2541
01:24:44,320 --> 01:24:45,760
People from Shandong
only look out for their own.

2542
01:24:45,760 --> 01:24:46,760
I guess that saying is true.

2543
01:24:49,440 --> 01:24:50,800
That spatula has already

2544
01:24:50,800 --> 01:24:53,080
been used for three dishes

2545
01:24:53,760 --> 01:24:54,720
without being washed.

2546
01:24:54,720 --> 01:24:56,600
(That is hardly a problem)
Your food's in mine, and mine's in yours.

2547
01:24:56,600 --> 01:24:57,400
We are all family here.

2548
01:24:57,400 --> 01:24:58,400
There is no need to be so formal.

2549
01:24:59,480 --> 01:24:59,960
Bing.

2550
01:25:02,120 --> 01:25:02,520
What is this?

2551
01:25:03,080 --> 01:25:03,840
Chicken and glass noodle stew.

2552
01:25:04,480 --> 01:25:04,760
All right.

2553
01:25:12,880 --> 01:25:13,640
How'd you manage to fall off

2554
01:25:13,640 --> 01:25:14,640
your chair while cooking?

2555
01:25:14,640 --> 01:25:15,280
Bing...

2556
01:25:16,040 --> 01:25:17,240
He kept stirring until he ended up

2557
01:25:17,240 --> 01:25:18,080
cooking in my pan.

2558
01:25:18,300 --> 01:25:19,900
(Everyone's dishes
are now mixed together)

2559
01:25:20,160 --> 01:25:21,000
(Add boiling water and noodles.
Simmer for 20 minutes)

2560
01:25:21,000 --> 01:25:22,060
Peel some potatoes, add the glass
noodles, and let the sauce reduce.

2561
01:25:23,020 --> 01:25:23,720
(Meanwhile, the mixed stew
is being stir-fried)

2562
01:25:23,720 --> 01:25:24,240
I will peel two.

2563
01:25:24,720 --> 01:25:25,760
Do you know how to peel them?

2564
01:25:26,760 --> 01:25:27,280
Do you know how to peel?

2565
01:25:27,280 --> 01:25:28,280
All I ever do is peel potatoes.

2566
01:25:28,280 --> 01:25:29,420
(Confidently taking charge)
All right, peel two potatoes.

2567
01:25:29,540 --> 01:25:30,540
(A familiar routine)

2568
01:25:33,360 --> 01:25:34,200
Everyone's been using these pots,

2569
01:25:34,200 --> 01:25:35,000
and now I'm stuck

2570
01:25:35,000 --> 01:25:36,080
with the big one.

2571
01:25:38,640 --> 01:25:39,480
Bai, it is your birthday today.

2572
01:25:39,480 --> 01:25:40,640
Bai.

2573
01:25:42,000 --> 01:25:42,880
I have already gotten
some water ready for you.

2574
01:25:42,880 --> 01:25:43,960
Come over and soak your feet.

2575
01:25:44,060 --> 01:25:46,140
(A special birthday ritual)

2576
01:25:48,320 --> 01:25:49,360
Take it over to Bai.

2577
01:25:51,220 --> 01:25:54,020
(Obediently following instructions)

2578
01:25:54,100 --> 01:25:55,180
(Waiting for the Northeastern
mixed stew)

2579
01:25:57,420 --> 01:25:58,620
(Add the pork belly
and stir-fry until fragrant)

2580
01:25:59,020 --> 01:26:00,780
(Add the vegetables one by one)

2581
01:26:00,960 --> 01:26:01,600
One has a strong smell,

2582
01:26:01,600 --> 01:26:02,720
(Add the seasonings)
while the other smells wonderful.

2583
01:26:04,660 --> 01:26:05,980
(Add boiling water
and let everything simmer)

2584
01:26:07,920 --> 01:26:08,760
What smells so good?

2585
01:26:09,040 --> 01:26:10,600
Could it be my cooking?

2586
01:26:10,940 --> 01:26:12,460
(You're giving yourself too much credit)
It doesn't seem to be mine after all.

2587
01:26:14,060 --> 01:26:15,920
(Let me have a look)

2588
01:26:15,920 --> 01:26:17,280
Is someone grilling something?

2589
01:26:21,360 --> 01:26:22,520
The way they are grilling it

2590
01:26:22,520 --> 01:26:23,240
is impressive.

2591
01:26:25,500 --> 01:26:26,660
(An early meal)

2592
01:26:29,980 --> 01:26:31,660
(How is everyone else doing?)

2593
01:26:32,480 --> 01:26:33,440
What smells so good?

2594
01:26:33,800 --> 01:26:34,200
This?

2595
01:26:36,080 --> 01:26:37,000
(A joint effort by Jia Bing,
Hu Xianxu, and Song Yaxuan)

2596
01:26:37,000 --> 01:26:37,910
The scallion-braised tofu is ready.

2597
01:26:37,910 --> 01:26:39,600
(Scallion-braised tofu is ready)
Bing, please give it a taste.

2598
01:26:43,600 --> 01:26:44,440
Is there anything wrong with it?

2599
01:26:44,440 --> 01:26:45,200
Nothing is wrong with it.

2600
01:26:45,720 --> 01:26:46,680
This is Michelin-worthy.

2601
01:26:47,760 --> 01:26:48,200
It is ready.

2602
01:26:48,480 --> 01:26:49,280
You made this?

2603
01:26:55,880 --> 01:26:56,800
You have improved so much!

2604
01:26:57,520 --> 01:26:58,680
Bing added the seasonings, though.

2605
01:26:58,680 --> 01:27:00,460
(Bing deserves most of the credit)

2606
01:27:00,720 --> 01:27:01,200
It is delicious.

2607
01:27:01,480 --> 01:27:02,000
Is it good?

2608
01:27:06,120 --> 01:27:06,480
Is it good?

2609
01:27:06,480 --> 01:27:06,720
Delicious.

2610
01:27:06,720 --> 01:27:07,320
The flavors have really
infused the dish.

2611
01:27:07,320 --> 01:27:07,840
Delicious.

2612
01:27:07,840 --> 01:27:08,360
It is excellent.

2613
01:27:10,940 --> 01:27:11,980
(Calling Wang Anyu)
Anyu.

2614
01:27:12,360 --> 01:27:14,120
Teng, are you eating?

2615
01:27:14,360 --> 01:27:15,080
You've been through a lot.

2616
01:27:16,000 --> 01:27:17,080
Oh, my goodness.

2617
01:27:17,080 --> 01:27:18,000
I feel for you.

2618
01:27:18,160 --> 01:27:19,640
I missed you, Teng.

2619
01:27:20,480 --> 01:27:21,320
You must have missed me.

2620
01:27:22,440 --> 01:27:23,560
Your favorite Bai

2621
01:27:23,960 --> 01:27:25,840
is on his way over.

2622
01:27:26,760 --> 01:27:28,520
Is this the birthday celebration?

2623
01:27:28,520 --> 01:27:34,480
♪Happy birthday to you♪

2624
01:27:35,520 --> 01:27:36,480
Come on, compliment me. Hurry.

2625
01:27:36,500 --> 01:27:37,720
(Fishing for compliments)
Say something nice.

2626
01:27:37,720 --> 01:27:38,600
Does he look handsome?

2627
01:27:38,600 --> 01:27:40,280
You do look a little more handsome.

2628
01:27:40,280 --> 01:27:41,240
You looked like a completely

2629
01:27:41,240 --> 01:27:43,120
(Better not to hear about it)
different person in Hengdian.

2630
01:27:45,480 --> 01:27:46,360
Come on, Anyu.

2631
01:27:46,360 --> 01:27:47,840
Say hello to everyone.

2632
01:27:48,120 --> 01:27:48,960
Ancient man.

2633
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:51,120
Chengcheng dyed his hair too.

2634
01:27:51,120 --> 01:27:53,120
Hello, Bing.

2635
01:27:53,720 --> 01:27:54,600
Churan.

2636
01:27:54,600 --> 01:27:55,400
Ancient man.

2637
01:27:55,400 --> 01:27:56,440
Mr. Huang.

2638
01:27:57,240 --> 01:27:57,920
Song.

2639
01:27:57,920 --> 01:27:58,560
Hello, Anyu.

2640
01:27:58,560 --> 01:27:59,640
Long time no see.

2641
01:27:59,640 --> 01:28:01,200
Were you surprised to see Song?

2642
01:28:01,380 --> 01:28:02,900
(Weak signal)

2643
01:28:03,320 --> 01:28:05,160
(Well...)
You do not have to hurry back.

2644
01:28:06,800 --> 01:28:08,640
Take care while filming.

2645
01:28:08,640 --> 01:28:09,600
I have to get back to filming.

2646
01:28:09,600 --> 01:28:11,520
I just called to say hello.
I have to go now.

2647
01:28:11,520 --> 01:28:12,280
All right.

2648
01:28:12,280 --> 01:28:13,080
Do your best, Anyu.

2649
01:28:13,080 --> 01:28:13,640
Good luck.

2650
01:28:13,640 --> 01:28:14,520
We all miss you.

2651
01:28:14,520 --> 01:28:15,320
Good luck.

2652
01:28:15,320 --> 01:28:15,880
All right.

2653
01:28:15,880 --> 01:28:16,240
Good luck.

2654
01:28:16,240 --> 01:28:16,800
All right.

2655
01:28:18,640 --> 01:28:19,320
Happy birthday, Bai.

2656
01:28:19,320 --> 01:28:21,080
Say something to Bai before you go.

2657
01:28:22,040 --> 01:28:24,520
Happy birthday to you.

2658
01:28:24,520 --> 01:28:25,840
You silly.

2659
01:28:25,840 --> 01:28:26,560
That did not sound sincere.

2660
01:28:26,560 --> 01:28:26,920
Hang up.

2661
01:28:28,760 --> 01:28:29,640
Bye, Anyu.

2662
01:28:29,640 --> 01:28:31,000
Goodbye, Teng.

2663
01:28:31,000 --> 01:28:31,800
Get some rest.

2664
01:28:34,300 --> 01:28:36,380
(The beef rice bowl is ready)

2665
01:28:37,800 --> 01:28:38,320
Song,

2666
01:28:39,360 --> 01:28:40,520
I do not have much for you,

2667
01:28:40,520 --> 01:28:41,360
just this bowl.

2668
01:28:41,800 --> 01:28:42,680
Beef rice bowl.

2669
01:28:47,800 --> 01:28:48,480
Bai,

2670
01:28:49,200 --> 01:28:50,600
I do not have much to give you either.

2671
01:28:50,600 --> 01:28:52,400
This bowl is all I have to offer.

2672
01:28:52,400 --> 01:28:53,120
Let me hold it for you.

2673
01:28:56,740 --> 01:29:02,700
(Hoping for a good review)

2674
01:29:04,520 --> 01:29:05,760
Quick, stop filming Bai.

2675
01:29:06,280 --> 01:29:07,480
Look at him devouring his food.

2676
01:29:07,620 --> 01:29:09,980
(Chef Fan is very pleased)

2677
01:29:11,920 --> 01:29:13,760
My chicken wings turned out great.

2678
01:29:14,200 --> 01:29:15,000
The chicken wings are delicious?

2679
01:29:15,720 --> 01:29:16,720
They turned out great.

2680
01:29:16,720 --> 01:29:17,560
They are ready.

2681
01:29:17,560 --> 01:29:18,980
(Wang Churan's cola chicken
wings are ready)

2682
01:29:19,040 --> 01:29:19,720
Here you go, Bai.

2683
01:29:19,720 --> 01:29:21,300
(An invitation to taste her cooking)

2684
01:29:21,400 --> 01:29:22,520
You just ate his food?

2685
01:29:23,480 --> 01:29:24,560
This might taste a little...

2686
01:29:24,560 --> 01:29:25,760
They taste different, right?

2687
01:29:25,760 --> 01:29:26,880
(That is unlikely)
No, they should not.

2688
01:29:26,880 --> 01:29:28,400
But they were made
with the same spatula.

2689
01:29:28,400 --> 01:29:28,840
It is hard to say.

2690
01:29:28,840 --> 01:29:29,440
Have you tried them?

2691
01:29:29,560 --> 01:29:30,400
Yes. They are delicious.

2692
01:29:35,880 --> 01:29:36,480
Delicious.

2693
01:29:36,480 --> 01:29:37,200
Not bad, right?

2694
01:29:37,200 --> 01:29:37,960
They are good.

2695
01:29:39,000 --> 01:29:39,520
Here you go, Teng.

2696
01:29:39,840 --> 01:29:40,520
Cola chicken wings?

2697
01:29:40,520 --> 01:29:40,840
Yes.

2698
01:29:41,440 --> 01:29:42,500
Since you made them,
I should try some.

2699
01:29:42,500 --> 01:29:43,260
(Showing his support)

2700
01:29:44,660 --> 01:29:45,880
(That is not what you said earlier)

2701
01:29:45,880 --> 01:29:47,800
I never eat chicken wings, Chengcheng.

2702
01:29:48,240 --> 01:29:49,640
Old people do not know any better.

2703
01:29:54,960 --> 01:29:55,640
How are they?

2704
01:29:56,720 --> 01:29:58,200
The flavor is almost

2705
01:29:58,200 --> 01:29:59,760
as if Chengcheng had lost

2706
01:29:59,760 --> 01:30:00,120
his recipe

2707
01:30:00,120 --> 01:30:01,240
and you happened to find it.

2708
01:30:03,200 --> 01:30:03,400
No.

2709
01:30:03,400 --> 01:30:05,600
We learned from the same online recipe.

2710
01:30:05,600 --> 01:30:07,040
We must have learned
from the same teacher.

2711
01:30:07,480 --> 01:30:09,400
Why are these chicken wings so sweet?

2712
01:30:10,360 --> 01:30:11,240
Still, they are pretty good.

2713
01:30:11,240 --> 01:30:12,000
Very tender.

2714
01:30:12,440 --> 01:30:13,520
Let me try Churan's.

2715
01:30:14,000 --> 01:30:14,360
Here.

2716
01:30:18,000 --> 01:30:18,560
They are not sticky.

2717
01:30:27,560 --> 01:30:28,440
Why do these chicken wings taste

2718
01:30:28,440 --> 01:30:29,560
